rotected branches,\nnot just stg and main.\n\nChanges:\n- Update .windsurfrules: all PRs require 1 review approval\n- dev ruleset updated to required_approving_review_count=1\n- main PR also requires CodeQL passing\n\nImpact: No code reaches any protected branch without a peer review.\n\n* 🔧 chore: branch protection, CloudBeaver, lifecycle rebuild/remove and infra fixes (#266)\n\n* 🔧 chore(git): require 1 review approval on all branches (dev/stg/main)\n\nEnforce code review with approval on all three protected branches,\nnot just stg and main.\n\nChanges:\n- Update .windsurfrules: all PRs require 1 review approval\n- dev ruleset updated to required_approving_review_count=1\n- main PR also requires CodeQL passing\n\nImpact: No code reaches any protected branch without a peer review.\n\n* 🔧 chore(cloudbeaver): seed data-sources template and patch forceHttps on startup\n\nAdd a data-sources.json template with env-interpolated PostgreSQL and MySQL\nconnections, copy it into the CloudBeaver image, and patch the runtime.conf\nfile to disable forceHttps on container startup.\n\nChanges:\n- Add config/cloudbeaver/data-sources.json template with envsubst vars\n- Copy template into /opt/cloudbeaver/conf-template/ in Dockerfile\n- Add forceHttps: false to cloudbeaver.conf.template\n- Patch .cloudbeaver.runtime.conf to disable forceHttps on each boot\n- Auto-seed data-sources.json into GlobalConfiguration/.dbeaver if absent\n\nImpact: CloudBeaver starts with pre-configured database connections and\nno HTTPS redirect loop on local/Docker environments\n\n* 🐛 fix(infra): correct PostgreSQL port references and restore hoppscotch-migrate\n\nPort was inconsistently set as 5432/5442 instead of 5542 (PG_EXTERNAL_PORT).\nUncomment and fix hoppscotch-migrate service to depend on correct DB port\nand wait for migration completion before starting the main app.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace hardcoded port 5432 with PG_EXTERNAL_PORT var in docker-compose.yml\n- Uncomment hoppscotch-migrate service and add it as dependency of hoppscotch\n- Fix postgres health-check port from 5442 to 5542 in health-check.service.ts\n- Fix DATABASE_URL key name and default port in service-schemas.ts\n\nImpact: Hoppscotch and health checks now connect to the correct PostgreSQL port\n\n* 🔧 chore(build): support cross-platform rollup native binding installation\n\nThe make setup target failed on Linux because the optional dependency\nwas pinned to darwin-arm64. Detect the libc suffix at runtime so the\ncorrect platform-specific package is installed on any OS.\n\nChanges:\n- Add LIBC variable detection in Makefile (empty on macOS, -gnu on Linux)\n- Append LIBC suffix to rollup native package name in setup target\n- Remove hardcoded @rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64 from optionalDependencies\n\nImpact: make setup works correctly on Linux (CI/CD) and macOS\n\n* ✨ feat(lifecycle): add rebuild and remove-container service actions\n\nServices sometimes need a full image rebuild (--build --force-recreate)\nor container removal without stopping the profile. Expose these as\ndedicated API endpoints with proper error handling and health tracking.\n\nChanges:\n- Add rebuildService() to DockerComposeService (stop + up --build --force-recreate)\n- Add removeContainer() to DockerComposeService (compose rm -sf)\n- Use --force-recreate when env overrides are present in startService()\n- Use --force-recreate in restartService() to pick up config changes\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() to ServiceLifecycleService\n- Expose POST /services/:id/rebuild and DELETE /services/:id/container endpoints\n- Add unit tests for rebuild and remove-container scenarios\n\nImpact: Users can force-rebuild service images and remove orphaned containers\nfrom the Settings panel\n\n* ✨ feat(settings-ui): add rebuild and remove-container actions to service cards\n\nExpose the new rebuild and remove-container lifecycle actions in the\nSettings dashboard. The remove button uses a double-click confirmation\npattern (3s timeout) to prevent accidental removals.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Hammer (rebuild) and Trash2 (remove) buttons to ServiceActions\n- Implement double-click confirmation pattern for container removal\n- Propagate onRebuild/onRemoveContainer props through ServiceGrid and ServiceCard\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() calls in useSettings hook\n- Fix verifyMasterPassword to read response.verified instead of response.success\n- Wire handlers in SettingsPage\n- Add i18n keys for rebuild and remove-container labels (en/es/pt)\n\nImpact: Users can trigger rebuild and remove from the service card action bar\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-snapshots): fix basename metadata key backward compatibility and partial updates\n\nMetadata was historically stored under the bare basename (no extension).\ngetSnapshotMeta now merges entries by full name and basename, and update()\nmigrates the old key to the full name while preserving existing field values\non partial updates.\n\nChanges:\n- Look up metadata by both full name and basename in getSnapshotMeta()\n- Merge fields from both entries with full-name taking precedence\n- Preserve existing metadata fields when partial updates are applied\n- Migrate basename key to full-name key after any update\n- Wrap psql restore in try/catch to throw descriptive error message\n- Add tests for backward-compat lookup, partial update preservation,\n  key migration, and psql restore failure message\n\nImpact: Snapshots created before the naming fix retain their metadata\nand update operations no longer silently reset unspecified fields\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-ui): throw error with message from API response body on failed requests\n\nSilent failures were masking real API errors. Extract message or error\nfield from the JSON body before falling back to a generic string.\n\nChanges:\n- Read data.message or data.error from response body before throwing\n\nImpact: API errors are surfaced correctly in the database UI\n\n* 🐛 fix(lifecycle): add error handling and configDb guard to rebuild/remove actions\n\nReview fixes for PR #266: rebuildService and removeContainer lacked\nres.ok checks in the UI hook, and missed the configDb.getService() guard\nin the API service (causing registry.getService() to throw for unknown services).\n\nChanges:\n- Add res.ok checks with descriptive errors in useSettings.ts rebuildService/removeContainer\n- Add configDb.getService() null-check guard before registry.getService() in both methods\n- Remove redundant as HealthStatus type assertions (type already includes disabled)\n\nLifecycle spec: 26/26 passing (was 24/26 before guard fix).\n\nImpact: Prevents silent UI failures and fixes 2 test failures in service lifecycle spec.\n\n* 🔖 chore(version): bump all packages to 2.6.3\n\nEqualize versions across the entire monorepo for release v2.6.3.\n\nChanges:\n- Bump root + shared, api, db-ui, mock-ui, ui from 2.6.2 to 2.6.3\n- Bump cli from 2.6.1 to 2.6.3\n- Bump vscode-extension from 2.3.0 to 2.6.3\n\nImpact: All packages now share the same version for consistent release tagging.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwIPFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT+gQACbMJOw6UF5szyUlipnKEeiL\nsODkvVQhnJk/88hytoSf5OuK0GeG49zZmGonJInRruoqgYBGU4dZpcBAnz4UOXQj\nDDo/0rrSKIPwsn4U61YtdLLKvnI9C9dw55B8qzZTRAzKc0MOCPSWAsgYivRkKRYZ\n7fkM95LirHLfMtSX2YuvjTQ8gc/SMSHZxmtyvmb2EM8jxkm9qFsojaPBKXSsTuYG\nsJVI7CJsZcNzqHw+TVi0LIKaYSCHh6wb5MB0ljsMFVPkokAgkwk06+69Tc+uLXq2\n90SSHWy3Lmxwr6xmdpjiZcvqdzwL07AY4PWqG50IqiaEvYhPVSdmthrtBc9p0bDE\nfmEBnw5y6mPMzCpBWF5OKjvMeAb/wNDDSZCF7H01Ej+d7g745NhGcl6TsJ1//fpy\npKudf57goby/Z5Lc5rPGBrTvTPgUghO3Ofcgt3VU2QxJHVtbSyOu5ijpVWEAErEd\n9uGQcHIgtkHM9325HuW7I+OZBX5RckOEx81q/v0i2iOfXltc+wwZjcvJSZ1WuCpE\nq0ntLOpKgcCpYj8KAvB9qnuNLsIROEViZZoTEY/9hJnQbCQGGDMP2CVesQEMer2J\nCX2PcQHZiPa+1KcpIRkuenXk8ulFG8mRJ3f1eYmX6AwTJOO9oPE204v6HjhxArRh\nV4Dl7VIVhTEPJf2AI3Sc\n=0Loo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-23T00:05:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.gi