:"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/2900550c34cd460b4a5a2da38c3b37691bb4c24a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T23:44:56Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T23:44:56Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"message":"🔖 chore(version): bump all packages to 2.6.3\n\nEqualize versions across the entire monorepo for release v2.6.3.\n\nChanges:\n- Bump root + shared, api, db-ui, mock-ui, ui from 2.6.2 to 2.6.3\n- Bump cli from 2.6.1 to 2.6.3\n- Bump vscode-extension from 2.3.0 to 2.6.3\n\nImpact: All packages now share the same version for consistent release tagging.","tree":{"sha":"6c194d6a3dc39f1ff8c46d7f6ac05779deec9fcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/6c194d6a3dc39f1ff8c46d7f6ac05779deec9fcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/2900550c34cd460b4a5a2da38c3b37691bb4c24a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/2900550c34cd460b4a5a2da38c3b37691bb4c24a","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDI5MDA1NTBjMzRjZDQ2MGI0YTVhMmRhMzhjM2IzNzY5MWJiNGMyNGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f","sha":"771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f"}],"sha":"2900550c34cd460b4a5a2da38c3b37691bb4c24a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/2900550c34cd460b4a5a2da38c3b37691bb4c24a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T23:38:15Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T23:38:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🔧 chore: branch protection, CloudBeaver, lifecycle rebuild/remove and infra fixes (#266)\n\n* 🔧 chore(git): require 1 review approval on all branches (dev/stg/main)\n\nEnforce code review with approval on all three protected branches,\nnot just stg and main.\n\nChanges:\n- Update .windsurfrules: all PRs require 1 review approval\n- dev ruleset updated to required_approving_review_count=1\n- main PR also requires CodeQL passing\n\nImpact: No code reaches any protected branch without a peer review.\n\n* 🔧 chore(cloudbeaver): seed data-sources template and patch forceHttps on startup\n\nAdd a data-sources.json template with env-interpolated PostgreSQL and MySQL\nconnections, copy it into the CloudBeaver image, and patch the runtime.conf\nfile to disable forceHttps on container startup.\n\nChanges:\n- Add config/cloudbeaver/data-sources.json template with envsubst vars\n- Copy template into /opt/cloudbeaver/conf-template/ in Dockerfile\n- Add forceHttps: false to cloudbeaver.conf.template\n- Patch .cloudbeaver.runtime.conf to disable forceHttps on each boot\n- Auto-seed data-sources.json into GlobalConfiguration/.dbeaver if absent\n\nImpact: CloudBeaver starts with pre-configured database connections and\nno HTTPS redirect loop on local/Docker environments\n\n* 🐛 fix(infra): correct PostgreSQL port references and restore hoppscotch-migrate\n\nPort was inconsistently set as 5432/5442 instead of 5542 (PG_EXTERNAL_PORT).\nUncomment and fix hoppscotch-migrate service to depend on correct DB port\nand wait for migration completion before starting the main app.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace hardcoded port 5432 with PG_EXTERNAL_PORT var in docker-compose.yml\n- Uncomment hoppscotch-migrate service and add it as dependency of hoppscotch\n- Fix postgres health-check port from 5442 to 5542 in health-check.service.ts\n- Fix DATABASE_URL key name and default port in service-schemas.ts\n\nImpact: Hoppscotch and health checks now connect to the correct PostgreSQL port\n\n* 🔧 chore(build): support cross-platform rollup native binding installation\n\nThe make setup target failed on Linux because the optional dependency\nwas pinned to darwin-arm64. Detect the libc suffix at runtime so the\ncorrect platform-specific package is installed on any OS.\n\nChanges:\n- Add LIBC variable detection in Makefile (empty on macOS, -gnu on Linux)\n- Append LIBC suffix to rollup native package name in setup target\n- Remove hardcoded @rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64 from optionalDependencies\n\nImpact: make setup works correctly on Linux (CI/CD) and macOS\n\n* ✨ feat(lifecycle): add rebuild and remove-container service actions\n\nServices sometimes need a full image rebuild (--build --force-recreate)\nor container removal without stopping the profile. Expose these as\ndedicated API endpoints with proper error handling and health tracking.\n\nChanges:\n- Add rebuildService() to DockerComposeService (stop + up --build --force-recreate)\n- Add removeContainer() to DockerComposeService (compose rm -sf)\n- Use --force-recreate when env overrides are present in startService()\n- Use --force-recreate in restartService() to pick up config changes\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() to ServiceLifecycleService\n- Expose POST /services/:id/rebuild and DELETE /services/:id/container endpoints\n- Add unit tests for rebuild and remove-container scenarios\n\nImpact: Users can force-rebuild service images and remove orphaned containers\nfrom the Settings panel\n\n* ✨ feat(settings-ui): add rebuild and remove-container actions to service cards\n\nExpose the new rebuild and remove-container lifecycle actions in the\nSettings dashboard. The remove button uses a double-click confirmation\npattern (3s timeout) to prevent accidental removals.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Hammer (rebuild) and Trash2 (remove) buttons to ServiceActions\n- Implement double-click confirmation pattern for container removal\n- Propagate onRebuild/onRemoveContainer props through ServiceGrid and ServiceCard\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() calls in useSettings hook\n- Fix verifyMasterPassword to read response.verified instead of response.success\n- Wire handlers in SettingsPage\n- Add i18n keys for rebuild and remove-container labels (en/es/pt)\n\nImpact: Users can trigger rebuild and remove from the service card action bar\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-snapshots): fix basename metadata key backward compatibility and partial updates\n\nMetadata was historically stored under the bare basename (no extension).\ngetSnapshotMeta now merges entries by full name and basename, and update()\nmigrates the old key to the full name while preserving existing field values\non partial updates.\n\nChanges:\n- Look up metadata by both full name and basename in getSnapshotMeta()\n- Merge fields from both entries with full-name taking precedence\n- Preserve existing metadata fields when partial updates are applied\n- Migrate basename key to full-name key after any update\n- Wrap psql restore in try/catch to throw descriptive error message\n- Add tests for backward-compat lookup, partial update preservation,\n  key migration, and psql restore failure message\n\nImpact: Snapshots created before the naming fix retain their metadata\nand update operations no longer silently reset unspecified fields\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-ui): throw error with message from API response body on failed requests\n\nSilent failures were masking real API errors. Extract message or error\nfield from the JSON body before falling back to a generic string.\n\nChanges:\n- Read data.message or data.error from response body before throwing\n\nImpact: API errors are surfaced correctly in the database UI\n\n* 🐛 fix(lifecycle): add error handling and configDb guard to rebuild/remove actions\n\nReview fixes for PR #266: rebuildService and removeContainer lacked\nres.ok checks in the UI hook, and missed the configDb.getService() guard\nin the API service (causing registry.getService() to throw for unknown services).\n\nChanges:\n- Add res.ok checks with descriptive errors in useSettings.ts rebuildService/removeContainer\n- Add configDb.getService() null-check guard before registry.getService() in both methods\n- Remove redundant as HealthStatus type assertions (type already includes disabled)\n\nLifecycle spec: 26/26 passing (was 24/26 before guard fix).\n\nImpact: Prevents silent UI failures and fixes 2 test failures in service lifecycle spec.","tree":{"sha":"fdeb22aaedbc5abfe0ca59fcdb2549314f890cdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/fdeb22aaedbc5abfe0ca59fcdb2549314f890cdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f","verification":{"payload":"tree fdeb22aaedbc5abfe0ca59fcdb2549314f890cdb\nparent 0f131741ef16da75b9c12aaf0ea5b913cf890771\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1774222695 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774222695 -0300\n\n🔧 chore: branch protection, CloudBeaver, lifecycle rebuild/remove and infra fixes (#266)\n\n* 🔧 chore(git): require 1 review approval on all branches (dev/stg/main)\n\nEnforce code review with approval on all three protected branches,\nnot just stg and main.\n\nChanges:\n- Update .windsurfrules: all PRs require 1 review approval\n- dev ruleset updated to required_approving_review_count=1\n- main PR also requires CodeQL passing\n\nImpact: No code reaches any protected branch without a peer review.\n\n* 🔧 chore(cloudbeaver): seed data-sources template and patch forceHttps on startup\n\nAdd a data-sources.json template with env-interpolated PostgreSQL and MySQL\nconnections, copy it into the CloudBeaver image, and patch the runtime.conf\nfile to disable forceHttps on container startup.\n\nChanges:\n- Add config/cloudbeaver/data-sources.json template with envsubst vars\n- Copy template into /opt/cloudbeaver/conf-template/ in Dockerfile\n- Add forceHttps: false to cloudbeaver.conf.template\n- Patch .cloudbeaver.runtime.conf to disable forceHttps on each boot\n- Auto-seed data-sources.json into GlobalConfiguration/.dbeaver if absent\n\nImpact: CloudBeaver starts with pre-configured database connections and\nno HTTPS redirect loop on local/Docker environments\n\n* 🐛 fix(infra): correct PostgreSQL port references and restore hoppscotch-migrate\n\nPort was inconsistently set as 5432/5442 instead of 5542 (PG_EXTERNAL_PORT).\nUncomment and fix hoppscotch-migrate service to depend on correct DB port\nand wait for migration completion before starting the main app.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace hardcoded port 5432 with PG_EXTERNAL_PORT var in docker-compose.yml\n- Uncomment hoppscotch-migrate service and add it as dependency of hoppscotch\n- Fix postgres health-check port from 5442 to 5542 in health-check.service.ts\n- Fix DATABASE_URL key name and default port in service-schemas.ts\n\nImpact: Hoppscotch and health checks now connect to the correct PostgreSQL port\n\n* 🔧 chore(build): support cross-platform rollup native binding installation\n\nThe make setup target failed on Linux because the optional dependency\nwas pinned to darwin-arm64. Detect the libc suffix at runtime so the\ncorrect platform-specific package is installed on any OS.\n\nChanges:\n- Add LIBC variable detection in Makefile (empty on macOS, -gnu on Linux)\n- Append LIBC suffix to rollup native package name in setup target\n- Remove hardcoded @rollup/rollup-darwin-arm64 from optionalDependencies\n\nImpact: make setup works correctly on Linux (CI/CD) and macOS\n\n* ✨ feat(lifecycle): add rebuild and remove-container service actions\n\nServices sometimes need a full image rebuild (--build --force-recreate)\nor container removal without stopping the profile. Expose these as\ndedicated API endpoints with proper error handling and health tracking.\n\nChanges:\n- Add rebuildService() to DockerComposeService (stop + up --build --force-recreate)\n- Add removeContainer() to DockerComposeService (compose rm -sf)\n- Use --force-recreate when env overrides are present in startService()\n- Use --force-recreate in restartService() to pick up config changes\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() to ServiceLifecycleService\n- Expose POST /services/:id/rebuild and DELETE /services/:id/container endpoints\n- Add unit tests for rebuild and remove-container scenarios\n\nImpact: Users can force-rebuild service images and remove orphaned containers\nfrom the Settings panel\n\n* ✨ feat(settings-ui): add rebuild and remove-container actions to service cards\n\nExpose the new rebuild and remove-container lifecycle actions in the\nSettings dashboard. The remove button uses a double-click confirmation\npattern (3s timeout) to prevent accidental removals.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Hammer (rebuild) and Trash2 (remove) buttons to ServiceActions\n- Implement double-click confirmation pattern for container removal\n- Propagate onRebuild/onRemoveContainer props through ServiceGrid and ServiceCard\n- Add rebuildService() and removeContainer() calls in useSettings hook\n- Fix verifyMasterPassword to read response.verified instead of response.success\n- Wire handlers in SettingsPage\n- Add i18n keys for rebuild and remove-container labels (en/es/pt)\n\nImpact: Users can trigger rebuild and remove from the service card action bar\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-snapshots): fix basename metadata key backward compatibility and partial updates\n\nMetadata was historically stored under the bare basename (no extension).\ngetSnapshotMeta now merges entries by full name and basename, and update()\nmigrates the old key to the full name while preserving existing field values\non partial updates.\n\nChanges:\n- Look up metadata by both full name and basename in getSnapshotMeta()\n- Merge fields from both entries with full-name taking precedence\n- Preserve existing metadata fields when partial updates are applied\n- Migrate basename key to full-name key after any update\n- Wrap psql restore in try/catch to throw descriptive error message\n- Add tests for backward-compat lookup, partial update preservation,\n  key migration, and psql restore failure message\n\nImpact: Snapshots created before the naming fix retain their metadata\nand update operations no longer silently reset unspecified fields\n\n* 🐛 fix(db-ui): throw error with message from API response body on failed requests\n\nSilent failures were masking real API errors. Extract message or error\nfield from the JSON body before falling back to a generic string.\n\nChanges:\n- Read data.message or data.error from response body before throwing\n\nImpact: API errors are surfaced correctly in the database UI\n\n* 🐛 fix(lifecycle): add error handling and configDb guard to rebuild/remove actions\n\nReview fixes for PR #266: rebuildService and removeContainer lacked\nres.ok checks in the UI hook, and missed the configDb.getService() guard\nin the API service (causing registry.getService() to throw for unknown services).\n\nChanges:\n- Add res.ok checks with descriptive errors in useSettings.ts rebuildService/removeContainer\n- Add configDb.getService() null-check guard before registry.getService() in both methods\n- Remove redundant as HealthStatus type assertions (type already includes disabled)\n\nLifecycle spec: 26/26 passing (was 24/26 before guard fix).\n\nImpact: Prevents silent UI failures and fixes 2 test failures in service lifecycle spec.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwH1nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtacQAGdnUbcSKT+ySxGgORxZzkIO\n9lStwR6kEsMydZhaL1thzm3p9JzSxVjREnJBmsgiDaVqnG6gLLwiZIdmf4MaPOFf\nI4UUw+i/JWVCXeIkYA94AnE/Ll0f/QRmEkZ2xb7OOIF7ZHJHLlFZj9+2vsMIiSU9\nBp0g3oyeFanJBabkA6/avWIQ14hS6u2exdtBFjJyWYFpVQZ7uenJVmoR5gWu+ZcR\n3VlnKgB9UUPRCrXYNLeXYwD/yWqpIbm5qbDz6eaRY1Vj51OLnXHARU4Y/XAEjsP8\n1/cPmy2v7gPuF+i6wHJhm52gsLqzjqF2dedAlfMiRj9k9FlTCE9w13obEm1NF/6R\nbNBjzsLzeRr4iX/ZL3Sc6ej6ccUpbSHXWI852FLKC5ae5YmYhhleq8vO9nKRVsZ2\nOfYQf/HE/UqUcoLhGLs42y57e16zD2d8e09t/h4URV8xQvdqOnLAdMkI3ehIpGeC\nFvmteB/8QauAsEEUzGAM9XgHEhSsBCUPwxzlrhyoIAR2Pq1L/rfS5Bma1pAr9SD7\ntz6/Uuxi2cBOXye+TkCPgDbgtGP+Gi3rG1nHKGDMWfApMNFe8ZAxp+QPRkLMANFK\nnclLTTZ6gmAIV4CyJSyoOjKm9/Frzf6RlYC6oQH1zB4dHvIH43aFzNT4CDOQ4Lzt\nA7c1gYoCSYVrzcWqKPYT\n=Lza9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-22T23:38:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDc3MWQ1NzU2YTlkNGEwMDhmNjNkMWI4OGQwMjQxNzFjOTRkMjg0MGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/0f131741ef16da75b9c12aaf0ea5b913cf890771","sha":"0f131741ef16da75b9c12aaf0ea5b913cf890771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/0f131741ef16da75b9c12aaf0ea5b913cf890771"}],"sha":"771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/771d5756a9d4a008f63d1b88d024171c94d2840f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34258399?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Victor-Fernandes","id":34258399,"login":"Victor-Fernandes","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjU4Mzk5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Victor-Fernandes","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/0be3f68df0ab0ee44b14f2e3611d6192a12b9264/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-22T22:40:44Z","email":"34258399+Victor-Fernandes@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Victor Fernandes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-22T22:40:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add MongoDB snapshot support (#259)\n\n* docs: add MongoDB feature specification\n\nAdd detailed MongoDB integration specification with implementation\nphases, etapas, and technical design decisions.\n\n* feat: add MongoDB support with mongodump/mongorestore snapshots\n\n- Add MongoDB 7 service to docker-compose.yml with profiles mongodb/databases\n- Install mongodb-database-tools in Dockerfile.api for mongodump/mongorestore\n- Create MongodbDriver implementing DatabaseDriverInterface\n  - Uses mongodb Node.js driver for connections and queries\n  - Implements createSnapshot/restoreSnapshot with --archive --gzip\n  - Uses --drop flag on restore to prevent data merge\n- Register MongodbDriver in DriverRegistryService and DatabasesModule\n- Update DbSnapshotsService to handle .archive.gz extension\n- Add MongoDB environment variables to .env.example\n- Update DTOs to accept ''mongodb'' as valid engine\n- Add Makefile targets: mongodb, mongodb-up, mongodb-down, mongodb-shell\n- Create unit tests for MongodbDriver\n- Update UI EngineSelector with MongoDB icon (🍃) and green color scheme\n- Update README.md to include MongoDB in database support\n- Create mongo-init.js initialization script with sample data\n\nImplements: docs/feat_mongoDB.md\n\n* feat(db-ui): add MongoDB support to ProjectDatabaseConfigs and SnapshotForm\n\n- Add MongoDB to ENGINE_DEFAULTS with default port 27017\n- Add MongoDB to ENGINE_STYLE with green badge and 🍃 icon\n- Create ENGINE_PORTS mapping for all database engines\n- Replace hardcoded port placeholders with ENGINE_PORTS lookup\n- Add MongoDB option to engine select dropdown\n- Add MongoDB label to SnapshotForm ENGINE_LABEL mapping\n\n* feat(mongodb): add MONGO_CONTAINER env var for container name reference\n\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER=stubrix-mongodb to .env.example\n- Enables consistent container name reference across docker-compose and API services\n- Aligns with existing container naming pattern (POSTGRES_CONTAINER, MYSQL_CONTAINER)\n\n* test(mongodb): add maxBuffer, 127.0.0.1 replacement, and empty stdout tests\n- Add maxBuffer verification for local mongorestore calls (512MB limit)\n- Add test for 127.0.0.1→host.docker.internal replacement in Docker exec URI\n- Add test for empty stdout handling (warn instead of throw)\n- Mock child_process and fs modules to isolate unit tests\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER to test config\n- Add jest.clearAllMocks() to beforeEach for clean test state\n\n* fix(mongodb): add docker exec fallback for mongodump/mongorestore when tools not in PATH\n- Add hasMongodumpLocal() to check if mongodump is available locally\n- Add docker exec fallback for createSnapshot/restoreSnapshot when local tools missing\n- Use spawnSync with stdin/stdout piping for docker exec archive transfer\n- Add --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway for cross-platform localhost access\n- Replace 127.0.0.1/localhost with host.docker.internal in docker exec URI\n- Add maxBuffer: 512MB\n\n* 🐛 fix(mongodb): remove invalid --add-host flag, use streaming, add guards\n\nCritical fix: --add-host is not a valid docker exec flag — crashes the\nfallback path. Docker exec now uses localhost URI (correct for in-container\nmongodump/mongorestore). Replaced spawnSync with streaming spawn to avoid\nbuffering entire archives in memory.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove --add-host from docker exec calls (Critical)\n- Use localhost URI for docker exec path instead of host.docker.internal\n- Add isConfigured() guard to listDatabases, getDatabaseInfo, executeQuery\n- Rename hasMongodumpLocal() → hasMongoToolsLocal() with caching and mongorestore check\n- Add runtime shape validation in executeQuery before unsafe cast\n- Replace execFileSync with async execFileAsync (local path)\n- Replace spawnSync with streaming spawn + pipe (docker path)\n- Translate Portuguese JSDoc/comments to English\n- Change buildUri from private to protected for testability\n\nImpact: Fixes critical docker exec crash, eliminates 512MB memory buffer,\nimproves error handling and code quality across the MongoDB driver.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): add .archive.gz to listSnapshotFiles filter\n\nMongoDB snapshots use .archive.gz extension but listSnapshotFiles() only\nmatched .sql and .db — making MongoDB snapshots invisible to the API.\n\nChanges:\n- Add .archive.gz to the file extension filter in listSnapshotFiles()\n\nImpact: MongoDB snapshots are now correctly listed and restorable via the API.\n\n* 🧪 test(mongodb): remove ESLint suppressions, add coverage for public methods\n\nRemoves file-level ESLint disable comments and replaces (driver as any)\nwith a TestableMongodbDriver subclass that exposes protected buildUri.\nAdds comprehensive test coverage for healthCheck, listDatabases,\ngetDatabaseInfo, executeQuery, and docker exec path assertions.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove 3 file-level eslint-disable comments\n- Add TestableMongodbDriver subclass for buildUri testing\n- Add mongodb module mock with MongoClient, ping, listDatabases, stats\n- Add tests for healthCheck (success, failure, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for listDatabases (filters system DBs, overrides, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for getDatabaseInfo (returns size + collections, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for executeQuery (success, malformed JSON, missing collection, unconfigured)\n- Update docker exec tests to assert no --add-host and localhost URI\n- Update child_process mock to match new execFile + spawn API\n\nImpact: Test coverage increases from ~40% to ~85% for MongodbDriver.\n\n* 🎨 style(mongo-init): translate Portuguese comment to English\n\nPolicy violation: source files must use English for all comments.\n\nChanges:\n- Translate Portuguese comment on line 2 to English\n\nImpact: Complies with project language policy.\n\n* 🔧 chore(docker): add MONGO_CONTAINER env var to stubrix service\n\nThe MongoDB driver reads MONGO_CONTAINER to identify the docker exec\ntarget container. Without this env var, the driver silently falls back\nto the hardcoded default which may differ from the actual container name.\n\nChanges:\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER: ${MONGO_CONTAINER:-stubrix-mongodb} to stubrix service\n\nImpact: Ensures docker exec fallback targets the correct MongoDB container.\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): fix MongoDB profile name typo mongoDb → mongodb\n\nThe README listed the Docker Compose profile as `mongoDb` but the actual\nprofile in docker-compose.yml and the Makefile target use `mongodb`.\n\nChanges:\n- Fix profile name from `mongoDb` to `mongodb` in the database profiles table\n\nImpact: Prevents copy/paste usage errors when starting MongoDB via Docker.\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): restore full README and fix mongoDb → mongodb typo\n\nPrevious commit accidentally replaced README with placeholder content.\nThis restores the full README and fixes the MongoDB profile name typo.\n\nChanges:\n- Restore full README.md content\n- Fix profile name from mongoDb to mongodb in database profiles table\n\nImpact: README is intact and profile name matches docker-compose.yml.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): use getSnapshotExtension in setSnapshotMeta for correct metadata key\n\nsetSnapshotMeta() used path.extname() which returns .gz for .archive.gz files,\ncausing MongoDB snapshot metadata to be stored under a wrong key and never found on lookup.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace path.extname() with getSnapshotExtension() for correct extension detection\n- Store metadata under full filename (name) instead of baseName to align with getSnapshotMeta() lookup\n\nImpact: MongoDB snapshot metadata (favorite, protected, category) is now correctly persisted and retrieved.\n\n* 🐛 fix(mongodb): wait for writeStream finish before resolving dockerExecMongodump\n\ndockerExecMongodump() resolved on child process close without waiting for the\nwriteStream to finish flushing, risking truncated snapshot files on slow disks.\n\nChanges:\n- Wait for both child close and writeStream finish events before resolving\n- Add writeStream error handler to catch disk write failures\n- Use settled flag to prevent double resolve/reject\n\nImpact: Prevents corrupted/truncated MongoDB snapshot files from being reported as successful.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): backward-compat metadata fallback and mongorestore error handlers\n\ngetSnapshotMeta() now checks both full name and legacy baseName keys,\npreventing metadata loss after the key format change. dockerExecMongorestore()\ngains readStream and child.stdin error handlers with settled flag.\n\nChanges:\n- Add baseName fallback in getSnapshotMeta() for pre-existing metadata entries\n- Add readStream.on(''error'') and child.stdin.on(''error'') in dockerExecMongorestore\n- Use settled flag pattern to prevent double resolve/reject\n\nImpact: Prevents metadata loss on upgrade and silent restore failures\n\n* 🧪 test(mongodb): fix writeStream finish callback and test isolation in Docker path tests\n\nTests now capture and invoke the writeStream finish event handler,\nmatching the updated dockerExecMongodump implementation that waits for\nboth child close and stream finish before resolving.\n\nChanges:\n- Update mockWriteStream.on to capture finish callback in both Docker tests\n- Trigger finishCb after closeCallback to resolve the promise correctly\n- Add missing execFileSync.mockImplementation to second Docker test for isolation\n- Remove unused eslint-disable directive for no-unsafe-return\n- Remove unnecessary type assertion on mongodb.MongoClient\n- Use jest.requireActual<typeof import(''fs'')> for type-safe fs mock spread\n\nImpact: Tests no longer depend on execution order and accurately model streaming behavior\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): correct Makefile commands in Quick Start and profiles table\n\nmake up and make record TARGET=<url> do not exist as Makefile targets.\nCorrected to make wiremock and make wiremock-record respectively.\n\nChanges:\n- Quick Start: make up → make wiremock\n- Mock Engines table: make up → make wiremock, make record TARGET=<url> → make wiremock-record\n\nImpact: Copy-paste from README now works correctly\n\n* 🔒 security(snapshots): sanitize dynamic property keys to fix CodeQL injection alert\n\nAdd SAFE_SNAPSHOT_NAME regex to validate snapshot names before using them\nas dynamic object keys, resolving the CodeQL \"Remote property injection\" alert.\n\nChanges:\n- Add SAFE_SNAPSHOT_NAME regex (/^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._-]*$/) as static property\n- Validate name in setSnapshotMeta() — reject unsafe names with ForbiddenException\n- Validate name in getSnapshotMeta() — return defaults for unsafe names\n- Validate newName/currentName in update() rename — skip metadata transfer for unsafe names\n\nImpact: Resolves CodeQL High severity alert blocking PR #259 merge\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Marcelo Davanço <marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br>","tree":{"sha":"baa168dd23e1655f1d2e91deb4293b82397cbead","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/baa168dd23e1655f1d2e91deb4293b82397cbead"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/0be3f68df0ab0ee44b14f2e3611d6192a12b9264","verification":{"payload":"tree baa168dd23e1655f1d2e91deb4293b82397cbead\nparent a8b22fda3e734a3ca4f3a3556911cc95bc0e69c5\nauthor Victor Fernandes <34258399+Victor-Fernandes@users.noreply.github.com> 1774219244 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774219244 -0300\n\nfeat: add MongoDB snapshot support (#259)\n\n* docs: add MongoDB feature specification\n\nAdd detailed MongoDB integration specification with implementation\nphases, etapas, and technical design decisions.\n\n* feat: add MongoDB support with mongodump/mongorestore snapshots\n\n- Add MongoDB 7 service to docker-compose.yml with profiles mongodb/databases\n- Install mongodb-database-tools in Dockerfile.api for mongodump/mongorestore\n- Create MongodbDriver implementing DatabaseDriverInterface\n  - Uses mongodb Node.js driver for connections and queries\n  - Implements createSnapshot/restoreSnapshot with --archive --gzip\n  - Uses --drop flag on restore to prevent data merge\n- Register MongodbDriver in DriverRegistryService and DatabasesModule\n- Update DbSnapshotsService to handle .archive.gz extension\n- Add MongoDB environment variables to .env.example\n- Update DTOs to accept ''mongodb'' as valid engine\n- Add Makefile targets: mongodb, mongodb-up, mongodb-down, mongodb-shell\n- Create unit tests for MongodbDriver\n- Update UI EngineSelector with MongoDB icon (🍃) and green color scheme\n- Update README.md to include MongoDB in database support\n- Create mongo-init.js initialization script with sample data\n\nImplements: docs/feat_mongoDB.md\n\n* feat(db-ui): add MongoDB support to ProjectDatabaseConfigs and SnapshotForm\n\n- Add MongoDB to ENGINE_DEFAULTS with default port 27017\n- Add MongoDB to ENGINE_STYLE with green badge and 🍃 icon\n- Create ENGINE_PORTS mapping for all database engines\n- Replace hardcoded port placeholders with ENGINE_PORTS lookup\n- Add MongoDB option to engine select dropdown\n- Add MongoDB label to SnapshotForm ENGINE_LABEL mapping\n\n* feat(mongodb): add MONGO_CONTAINER env var for container name reference\n\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER=stubrix-mongodb to .env.example\n- Enables consistent container name reference across docker-compose and API services\n- Aligns with existing container naming pattern (POSTGRES_CONTAINER, MYSQL_CONTAINER)\n\n* test(mongodb): add maxBuffer, 127.0.0.1 replacement, and empty stdout tests\n- Add maxBuffer verification for local mongorestore calls (512MB limit)\n- Add test for 127.0.0.1→host.docker.internal replacement in Docker exec URI\n- Add test for empty stdout handling (warn instead of throw)\n- Mock child_process and fs modules to isolate unit tests\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER to test config\n- Add jest.clearAllMocks() to beforeEach for clean test state\n\n* fix(mongodb): add docker exec fallback for mongodump/mongorestore when tools not in PATH\n- Add hasMongodumpLocal() to check if mongodump is available locally\n- Add docker exec fallback for createSnapshot/restoreSnapshot when local tools missing\n- Use spawnSync with stdin/stdout piping for docker exec archive transfer\n- Add --add-host=host.docker.internal:host-gateway for cross-platform localhost access\n- Replace 127.0.0.1/localhost with host.docker.internal in docker exec URI\n- Add maxBuffer: 512MB\n\n* 🐛 fix(mongodb): remove invalid --add-host flag, use streaming, add guards\n\nCritical fix: --add-host is not a valid docker exec flag — crashes the\nfallback path. Docker exec now uses localhost URI (correct for in-container\nmongodump/mongorestore). Replaced spawnSync with streaming spawn to avoid\nbuffering entire archives in memory.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove --add-host from docker exec calls (Critical)\n- Use localhost URI for docker exec path instead of host.docker.internal\n- Add isConfigured() guard to listDatabases, getDatabaseInfo, executeQuery\n- Rename hasMongodumpLocal() → hasMongoToolsLocal() with caching and mongorestore check\n- Add runtime shape validation in executeQuery before unsafe cast\n- Replace execFileSync with async execFileAsync (local path)\n- Replace spawnSync with streaming spawn + pipe (docker path)\n- Translate Portuguese JSDoc/comments to English\n- Change buildUri from private to protected for testability\n\nImpact: Fixes critical docker exec crash, eliminates 512MB memory buffer,\nimproves error handling and code quality across the MongoDB driver.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): add .archive.gz to listSnapshotFiles filter\n\nMongoDB snapshots use .archive.gz extension but listSnapshotFiles() only\nmatched .sql and .db — making MongoDB snapshots invisible to the API.\n\nChanges:\n- Add .archive.gz to the file extension filter in listSnapshotFiles()\n\nImpact: MongoDB snapshots are now correctly listed and restorable via the API.\n\n* 🧪 test(mongodb): remove ESLint suppressions, add coverage for public methods\n\nRemoves file-level ESLint disable comments and replaces (driver as any)\nwith a TestableMongodbDriver subclass that exposes protected buildUri.\nAdds comprehensive test coverage for healthCheck, listDatabases,\ngetDatabaseInfo, executeQuery, and docker exec path assertions.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove 3 file-level eslint-disable comments\n- Add TestableMongodbDriver subclass for buildUri testing\n- Add mongodb module mock with MongoClient, ping, listDatabases, stats\n- Add tests for healthCheck (success, failure, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for listDatabases (filters system DBs, overrides, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for getDatabaseInfo (returns size + collections, unconfigured)\n- Add tests for executeQuery (success, malformed JSON, missing collection, unconfigured)\n- Update docker exec tests to assert no --add-host and localhost URI\n- Update child_process mock to match new execFile + spawn API\n\nImpact: Test coverage increases from ~40% to ~85% for MongodbDriver.\n\n* 🎨 style(mongo-init): translate Portuguese comment to English\n\nPolicy violation: source files must use English for all comments.\n\nChanges:\n- Translate Portuguese comment on line 2 to English\n\nImpact: Complies with project language policy.\n\n* 🔧 chore(docker): add MONGO_CONTAINER env var to stubrix service\n\nThe MongoDB driver reads MONGO_CONTAINER to identify the docker exec\ntarget container. Without this env var, the driver silently falls back\nto the hardcoded default which may differ from the actual container name.\n\nChanges:\n- Add MONGO_CONTAINER: ${MONGO_CONTAINER:-stubrix-mongodb} to stubrix service\n\nImpact: Ensures docker exec fallback targets the correct MongoDB container.\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): fix MongoDB profile name typo mongoDb → mongodb\n\nThe README listed the Docker Compose profile as `mongoDb` but the actual\nprofile in docker-compose.yml and the Makefile target use `mongodb`.\n\nChanges:\n- Fix profile name from `mongoDb` to `mongodb` in the database profiles table\n\nImpact: Prevents copy/paste usage errors when starting MongoDB via Docker.\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): restore full README and fix mongoDb → mongodb typo\n\nPrevious commit accidentally replaced README with placeholder content.\nThis restores the full README and fixes the MongoDB profile name typo.\n\nChanges:\n- Restore full README.md content\n- Fix profile name from mongoDb to mongodb in database profiles table\n\nImpact: README is intact and profile name matches docker-compose.yml.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): use getSnapshotExtension in setSnapshotMeta for correct metadata key\n\nsetSnapshotMeta() used path.extname() which returns .gz for .archive.gz files,\ncausing MongoDB snapshot metadata to be stored under a wrong key and never found on lookup.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace path.extname() with getSnapshotExtension() for correct extension detection\n- Store metadata under full filename (name) instead of baseName to align with getSnapshotMeta() lookup\n\nImpact: MongoDB snapshot metadata (favorite, protected, category) is now correctly persisted and retrieved.\n\n* 🐛 fix(mongodb): wait for writeStream finish before resolving dockerExecMongodump\n\ndockerExecMongodump() resolved on child process close without waiting for the\nwriteStream to finish flushing, risking truncated snapshot files on slow disks.\n\nChanges:\n- Wait for both child close and writeStream finish events before resolving\n- Add writeStream error handler to catch disk write failures\n- Use settled flag to prevent double resolve/reject\n\nImpact: Prevents corrupted/truncated MongoDB snapshot files from being reported as successful.\n\n* 🐛 fix(snapshots): backward-compat metadata fallback and mongorestore error handlers\n\ngetSnapshotMeta() now checks both full name and legacy baseName keys,\npreventing metadata loss after the key format change. dockerExecMongorestore()\ngains readStream and child.stdin error handlers with settled flag.\n\nChanges:\n- Add baseName fallback in getSnapshotMeta() for pre-existing metadata entries\n- Add readStream.on(''error'') and child.stdin.on(''error'') in dockerExecMongorestore\n- Use settled flag pattern to prevent double resolve/reject\n\nImpact: Prevents metadata loss on upgrade and silent restore failures\n\n* 🧪 test(mongodb): fix writeStream finish callback and test isolation in Docker path tests\n\nTests now capture and invoke the writeStream finish event handler,\nmatching the updated dockerExecMongodump implementation that waits for\nboth child close and stream finish before resolving.\n\nChanges:\n- Update mockWriteStream.on to capture finish callback in both Docker tests\n- Trigger finishCb after closeCallback to resolve the promise correctly\n- Add missing execFileSync.mockImplementation to second Docker test for isolation\n- Remove unused eslint-disable directive for no-unsafe-return\n- Remove unnecessary type assertion on mongodb.MongoClient\n- Use jest.requireActual<typeof import(''fs'')> for type-safe fs mock spread\n\nImpact: Tests no longer depend on execution order and accurately model streaming behavior\n\n* 📝 docs(readme): correct Makefile commands in Quick Start and profiles table\n\nmake up and make record TARGET=<url> do not exist as Makefile targets.\nCorrected to make wiremock and make wiremock-record respectively.\n\nChanges:\n- Quick Start: make up → make wiremock\n- Mock Engines table: make up → make wiremock, make record TARGET=<url> → make wiremock-record\n\nImpact: Copy-paste from README now works correctly\n\n* 🔒 security(snapshots): sanitize dynamic property keys to fix CodeQL injection alert\n\nAdd SAFE_SNAPSHOT_NAME regex to validate snapshot names before using them\nas dynamic object keys, resolving the CodeQL \"Remote property injection\" alert.\n\nChanges:\n- Add SAFE_SNAPSHOT_NAME regex (/^[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._-]*$/) as static property\n- Validate name in setSnapshotMeta() — reject unsafe names with ForbiddenException\n- Validate name in getSnapshotMeta() — return defaults for unsafe names\n- Validate newName/currentName in update() rename — skip metadata transfer for unsafe names\n\nImpact: Resolves CodeQL High severity alert blocking PR #259 merge\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Marcelo Davanço <marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpwG/sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0QUQAA+yt0Pfi7TQb1xZECakqYXV\nAG5lw/xmR1T+luZL+vHjv2Ef2ol7Sv5bXH6Ugf3epCybbTs7XfWAuepq7Bn6EGH/\nvBTgMWrxxuTgR8seWMubhrVo1n0Jmnq2075tuMD4MIC7zjs4O3+FNVHOIg1ExoND\nnZMrj0yxHypt/GIRy1tbmivrerU7198vZwoix7dUR3BDFdrb/eDAxuK+vnQDEHkl\nJDrmaceh/XMc6WgY5C9RlwLtfedr31gJy497yrqBHVMRKuZcGuTlvPD81raZs3sU\nxY7DpFaV+YXtTOyrcW5TxuMvdphGz2lc6Sw4lZTgksp+kVBXsuOiKknnsPXT0Zmr\nDL9VnUYUOW7FTRDkr20tAXpW7K7Rwd/Y5ufIdr7BvlQ3P1gCMKhGYWvXND7UgKkQ\njEHKygmy5Qzbq7c4X1520mfJvYtKwaD+iVN+oXSxbzuwgMB6j9Xk6lni0049oz4W\ncYsvTT8fbepO6fQCeaEj5ctRG0fEzbX1TRP2T1wG8aqFpIHhrKqoXX2qYeYuqcQA\nskiDTfOKadz7hV8VtW8T80BqrfkgrcGkXbNTjOHUl4bq/2Elyg+tU640Xvbm4cTA\n74M1aL9nB9OFVEbH285Bj+BitkblOvc6LA0fWt8MgqxgUktNhqQ5LcZgfQdHew8L\neoNiUBBgkDeK+9GZCBir\n=zO6Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-22T22:40:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.