brix/commits/a23c3a49a4da3be69c87b78f8ef1b92493ab7740"}],"sha":"4e28014319b0243014a8540746f81a66977fba62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/4e28014319b0243014a8540746f81a66977fba62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/a23c3a49a4da3be69c87b78f8ef1b92493ab7740/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-15T23:21:53Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-15T23:21:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🔒 fix: address code scanning alerts — remove unused imports, fix TypeScript errors, update vulnerable deps (#249)\n\n* 🧪 test(settings): fix missing auto_start field and migration assertions\n\nAdd missing auto_start property to ServiceRow fixtures in 3 spec files\n(11 TypeScript errors). Update schema version and totalRows assertions\nto reflect migration v2 which adds the auto_start column.\n\nChanges:\n- Add auto_start: 0|1 to all upsertService() fixtures in config-database.service.spec.ts\n- Add auto_start: 0 to seedService() in audit-log.service.spec.ts\n- Add auto_start: 0 to both upsertService() calls in integrity.service.spec.ts\n- Fix getSchemaVersion() assertions from 1 to 2 (migration v2 applied)\n- Fix totalRows assertion from 1 to 2 (schema_version now has 2 rows)\n- Fix enabled assertion in CRUD test (upsertService does not update enabled on conflict)\n\nImpact: Resolves 11 TS-001 TypeScript compile errors and aligns spec assertions\nwith current migration state.\n\n* 🔒 fix(api): remove unused imports and replace any type in recording service\n\nRemove unused imports flagged by CodeQL/ESLint (SEC-001/002). Replace\nunsafe any type in recording.service.ts with a typed WireMock mapping\ninterface to address CodeQL unsafe-assignment alerts (SEC-003).\n\nChanges:\n- Remove unused execFileSync import from recording.service.ts\n- Add typed interface for WireMock mapping GET response (replaces any)\n- Remove unused Patch import from auth.controller.ts\n- Remove unused UnauthorizedException import from auth.service.ts\n\nImpact: Eliminates CodeQL code scanning alerts for unsafe imports and\nuntyped external data access.\n\n* 🎨 style(api): apply prettier formatting to chaos-network files\n\nFix prettier/prettier ESLint errors in chaos-network controller and\nservice detected by code scanning.\n\nChanges:\n- Format chaos-network.controller.ts per prettier config\n- Format chaos-network.service.ts per prettier config\n\nImpact: Clears prettier/prettier code scanning style alerts.\n\n* 🔧 chore(deps): update vulnerable dependencies and add npm overrides\n\nAddress npm audit vulnerabilities: bump @usebruno/cli and inquirer,\nadd overrides to force safe versions of fast-xml-parser, minimatch,\nand file-type. Reduces vulnerability count from 39 to 15 (critical: 18→0, low: 5→0).\n\nChanges:\n- Bump @usebruno/cli from ^1.4.0 to ^3.1.3 (root devDep)\n- Bump inquirer from ^10.2.2 to ^13.3.2 in @stubrix/cli (unused vestigial dep)\n- Add overrides: fast-xml-parser@^5.5.5 (fixes 18 critical AWS SDK chain)\n- Add overrides: minimatch@^10.2.4 (addresses ReDoS in transitive deps)\n- Add overrides: file-type@^21.3.2 (addresses DoS via @nestjs/common)\n- Regenerate package-lock.json\n\nRemaining 15 (5 high, 10 moderate): false positives where npm audit\nsuggests older versions as fix (@stoplight/spectral-*, @nestjs/cli),\nor no-fix-available (@vscode/vsce + yauzl, dev-only).\n\nImpact: Eliminates all 18 critical and 5 low severity vulnerabilities.\n\n* 🔖 chore(version): bump version 2.6.0 → 2.6.1\n\nPatch release addressing code scanning alerts: unused imports,\nTypeScript errors, any type usage, and npm dependency vulnerabilities.\n\nChanges:\n- Root and all packages bumped from 2.6.0 to 2.6.1\n\nImpact: Prepares release v2.6.1 for npm publish.\n\n* 🔖 chore(version): bump @stubrix/cli 2.6.0 → 2.6.1\n\n* 🔒 fix(chaos-network): sanitize URL path segments to prevent SSRF\n\nApply encodeURIComponent() to all user-controlled path segments used in\nfetch() calls to the Toxiproxy API, preventing path traversal and SSRF\ninjection via proxyName and toxicName parameters (CodeQL alerts 113, 114).\n\nChanges:\n- encodeURIComponent(proxyName) in addToxic()\n- encodeURIComponent(proxyName) and encodeURIComponent(toxicName) in removeToxic()\n- encodeURIComponent(name) in deleteProxy()\n\nImpact: Resolves 2 SSRF code scanning alerts on PR #249.","tree":{"sha":"bd46f755de1d7dd4fae6955f2c5f62c185225c8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/bd46f755de1d7dd4fae6955f2c5f62c185225c8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/a23c3a49a4da3be69c87b78f8ef1b92493ab7740","verification":{"payload":"tree bd46f755de1d7dd4fae6955f2c5f62c185225c8b\nparent 1db3891ecd3ea01a3f34ac6a13d8e0f4921c7306\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773616913 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773616913 -0300\n\n🔒 fix: address code scanning alerts — remove unused imports, fix TypeScript errors, update vulnerable deps (#249)\n\n* 🧪 test(settings): fix missing auto_start field and migration assertions\n\nAdd missing auto_start property to ServiceRow fixtures in 3 spec files\n(11 TypeScript errors). Update schema version and totalRows assertions\nto reflect migration v2 which adds the auto_start column.\n\nChanges:\n- Add auto_start: 0|1 to all upsertService() fixtures in config-database.service.spec.ts\n- Add auto_start: 0 to seedService() in audit-log.service.spec.ts\n- Add auto_start: 0 to both upsertService() calls in integrity.service.spec.ts\n- Fix getSchemaVersion() assertions from 1 to 2 (migration v2 applied)\n- Fix totalRows assertion from 1 to 2 (schema_version now has 2 rows)\n- Fix enabled assertion in CRUD test (upsertService does not update enabled on conflict)\n\nImpact: Resolves 11 TS-001 TypeScript compile errors and aligns spec assertions\nwith current migration state.\n\n* 🔒 fix(api): remove unused imports and replace any type in recording service\n\nRemove unused imports flagged by CodeQL/ESLint (SEC-001/002). Replace\nunsafe any type in recording.service.ts with a typed WireMock mapping\ninterface to address CodeQL unsafe-assignment alerts (SEC-003).\n\nChanges:\n- Remove unused execFileSync import from recording.service.ts\n- Add typed interface for WireMock mapping GET response (replaces any)\n- Remove unused Patch import from auth.controller.ts\n- Remove unused UnauthorizedException import from auth.service.ts\n\nImpact: Eliminates CodeQL code scanning alerts for unsafe imports and\nuntyped external data access.\n\n* 🎨 style(api): apply prettier formatting to chaos-network files\n\nFix prettier/prettier ESLint errors in chaos-network controller and\nservice detected by code scanning.\n\nChanges:\n- Format chaos-network.controller.ts per prettier config\n- Format chaos-network.service.ts per prettier config\n\nImpact: Clears prettier/prettier code scanning style alerts.\n\n* 🔧 chore(deps): update vulnerable dependencies and add npm overrides\n\nAddress npm audit vulnerabilities: bump @usebruno/cli and inquirer,\nadd overrides to force safe versions of fast-xml-parser, minimatch,\nand file-type. Reduces vulnerability count from 39 to 15 (critical: 18→0, low: 5→0).\n\nChanges:\n- Bump @usebruno/cli from ^1.4.0 to ^3.1.3 (root devDep)\n- Bump inquirer from ^10.2.2 to ^13.3.2 in @stubrix/cli (unused vestigial dep)\n- Add overrides: fast-xml-parser@^5.5.5 (fixes 18 critical AWS SDK chain)\n- Add overrides: minimatch@^10.2.4 (addresses ReDoS in transitive deps)\n- Add overrides: file-type@^21.3.2 (addresses DoS via @nestjs/common)\n- Regenerate package-lock.json\n\nRemaining 15 (5 high, 10 moderate): false positives where npm audit\nsuggests older versions as fix (@stoplight/spectral-*, @nestjs/cli),\nor no-fix-available (@vscode/vsce + yauzl, dev-only).\n\nImpact: Eliminates all 18 critical and 5 low severity vulnerabilities.\n\n* 🔖 chore(version): bump version 2.6.0 → 2.6.1\n\nPatch release addressing code scanning alerts: unused imports,\nTypeScript errors, any type usage, and npm dependency vulnerabilities.\n\nChanges:\n- Root and all packages bumped from 2.6.0 to 2.6.1\n\nImpact: Prepares release v2.6.1 for npm publish.\n\n* 🔖 chore(version): bump @stubrix/cli 2.6.0 → 2.6.1\n\n* 🔒 fix(chaos-network): sanitize URL path segments to prevent SSRF\n\nApply encodeURIComponent() to all user-controlled path segments used in\nfetch() calls to the Toxiproxy API, preventing path traversal and SSRF\ninjection via proxyName and toxicName parameters (CodeQL alerts 113, 114).\n\nChanges:\n- encodeURIComponent(proxyName) in addToxic()\n- encodeURIComponent(proxyName) and encodeURIComponent(toxicName) in removeToxic()\n- encodeURIComponent(name) in deleteProxy()\n\nImpact: Resolves 2 SSRF code scanning alerts on PR #249.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BE