9f8917e","sha":"dd3f1eb026c71ce6fb2bae9149bcea5039f8917e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/dd3f1eb026c71ce6fb2bae9149bcea5039f8917e"}],"sha":"a241a4d5e7447c8da3818800aba613e8aaa56ed6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/a241a4d5e7447c8da3818800aba613e8aaa56ed6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/dd3f1eb026c71ce6fb2bae9149bcea5039f8917e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T16:05:27Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T16:05:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(infra): fix Zitadel crash-loop by configuring PostgreSQL connection (#245)\n\n* 🐛 fix(infra): fix Zitadel crash-loop by configuring PostgreSQL connection\n\nZitadel was crash-looping because it tried to connect to localhost:5432\ninstead of the db-postgres Docker service. No PostgreSQL env vars were set\nand there was no depends_on to sequence startup.\n\nChanges:\n- Add ZITADEL_DATABASE_POSTGRES_* env vars pointing to db-postgres service\n- Add ZITADEL_EXTERNALDOMAIN, ZITADEL_EXTERNALPORT, ZITADEL_EXTERNALPROTOCOL\n- Add depends_on: db-postgres (condition: service_healthy, required: false)\n- Update Zitadel service definition dependsOn to include postgres\n- Add ZITADEL_DB to .env.example with usage note\n\nTechnical: start with both profiles:\n  docker compose --profile zitadel --profile postgres up -d\n\nImpact: Zitadel initializes correctly and connects to PostgreSQL on startup\n\n* ✨ feat(settings): inject config DB values as env overrides on docker compose up\n\nServices configured via the Settings panel now have their config values\ninjected as process env overrides when docker compose starts the container.\nDocker compose resolves ${VAR:-default} substitutions using these values.\n\nChanges:\n- Add envOverrides param to DockerComposeService.startService/startProfile\n- Pass env overrides to execFile via process.env spread so compose resolves vars\n- Add buildEnvOverrides() to ServiceLifecycleService — reads service configs from SQLite\n- Pass overrides to startService, startProfile, and companion startService calls\n- Add PostgreSQL connection fields to ZITADEL_CONFIG_SCHEMA (host, port, db, user, password)\n- Update docker-compose.yml Zitadel section to use ${ZITADEL_DATABASE_POSTGRES_*:-default} vars\n\nImpact: Settings panel can now configure external services without editing .env or docker-compose.yml directly","tree":{"sha":"2fefc4e07d61f4952494d2f55ea3a3e45c670ceb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/2fefc4e07d61f4952494d2f55ea3a3e45c670ceb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/dd3f1eb026c71ce6fb2bae9149bcea5039f8917e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2fefc4e07d61f4952494d2f55ea3a3e45c670ceb\nparent 05df0ceb21896ee567b56f13db13c4933dae36eb\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773504327 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773504327 -0300\n\nfix(infra): fix Zitadel crash-loop by configuring PostgreSQL connection (#245)\n\n* 🐛 fix(infra): fix Zitadel crash-loop by configuring PostgreSQL connection\n\nZitadel was crash-looping because it tried to connect to localhost:5432\ninstead of the db-postgres Docker service. No PostgreSQL env vars were set\nand there was no depends_on to sequence startup.\n\nChanges:\n- Add ZITADEL_DATABASE_POSTGRES_* env vars pointing to db-postgres service\n- Add ZITADEL_EXTERNALDOMAIN, ZITADEL_EXTERNALPORT, ZITADEL_EXTERNALPROTOCOL\n- Add depends_on: db-postgres (condition: service_healthy, required: false)\n- Update Zitadel service definition dependsOn to include postgres\n- Add ZITADEL_DB to .env.example with usage note\n\nTechnical: start with both profiles:\n  docker compose --profile zitadel --profile postgres up -d\n\nImpact: Zitadel initializes correctly and connects to PostgreSQL on startup\n\n* ✨ feat(settings): inject config DB values as env overrides on docker compose up\n\nServices configured via the Settings panel now have their config values\ninjected as process env overrides when docker compose starts the container.\nDocker compose resolves ${VAR:-default} substitutions using these values.\n\nChanges:\n- Add envOverrides param to DockerComposeService.startService/startProfile\n- Pass env overrides to execFile via process.env spread so compose resolves vars\n- Add buildEnvOverrides() to ServiceLifecycleService — reads service configs from SQLite\n- Pass overrides to startService, startProfile, and companion startService calls\n- Add PostgreSQL connection fields to ZITADEL_CONFIG_SCHEMA (host, port, db, user, password)\n- Update docker-compose.yml Zitadel section to use ${ZITADEL_DATABASE_POSTGRES_*:-default} vars\n\nImpact: Settings panel can now configure external services without editing .env or docker-compos