r UI root (/) can redirect or serve HTML slowly.\nThe Query API /api/services always returns JSON 200 immediately when running.\n\nChanges:\n- Update jaeger health check URL from / to /api/services\n\nImpact: Jaeger reports healthy correctly when container is running","tree":{"sha":"57ae45179bcbda85d09171c7b8f7da0b7a5d4c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/57ae45179bcbda85d09171c7b8f7da0b7a5d4c5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/05df0ceb21896ee567b56f13db13c4933dae36eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/05df0ceb21896ee567b56f13db13c4933dae36eb","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDA1ZGYwY2ViMjE4OTZlZTU2N2I1NmYxM2RiMTNjNDkzM2RhZTM2ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019","sha":"1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019"}],"sha":"05df0ceb21896ee567b56f13db13c4933dae36eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/05df0ceb21896ee567b56f13db13c4933dae36eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:34:53Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:34:53Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"message":"🐛 fix(health-check): add Basic Auth support for RabbitMQ health endpoint\n\nThe RabbitMQ Management API /api/healthchecks/node requires Basic Auth.\nhttpCheck was sending unauthenticated requests, receiving HTTP 401,\nand marking the service as unhealthy even when running correctly.\n\nChanges:\n- Add optional auth field to HttpCheckConfig interface\n- Update httpCheck to build Authorization: Basic header when auth is provided\n- Add auth: { username: guest, password: guest } to rabbitmq check config\n\nImpact: RabbitMQ reports healthy when the container is running and reachable","tree":{"sha":"2ef36069d481437681138b0be4defbdbe83e1423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/2ef36069d481437681138b0be4defbdbe83e1423"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDFmZTIwNTg1ODAwNTE4NzM3Y2Q3YmVhY2M3NWJmYjIyNzQyN2EwMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2","sha":"893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2"}],"sha":"1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/1fe20585800518737cd7beacc75bfb227427a019"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:23:51Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:23:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat(lifecycle): stop/start companion docker services with parent service (#244)\n\nWhen a service like OpenRAG has companion containers (openrag-langflow,\nopenrag-opensearch), disabling/enabling the parent left companions running\nor failed to start them alongside the main container.\n\nChanges:\n- Add dockerCompanions?: string[] field to ServiceDefinitionSeed in @stubrix/shared\n- Add dockerCompanions to openrag service definition (langflow + opensearch)\n- Add getCompanions(serviceId) method to ServiceRegistryService\n- Update enableService to start companions after the main container starts\n- Update disableService to stop companions before stopping the main container\n\nImpact: Disabling OpenRAG from the Settings panel now correctly stops\nall three containers (openrag, openrag-langflow, openrag-opensearch)","tree":{"sha":"b382c4155bc895308f4ae2a967a9428deea57180","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/b382c4155bc895308f4ae2a967a9428deea57180"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2","verification":{"payload":"tree b382c4155bc895308f4ae2a967a9428deea57180\nparent 318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773462231 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773462231 -0300\n\n✨ feat(lifecycle): stop/start companion docker services with parent service (#244)\n\nWhen a service like OpenRAG has companion containers (openrag-langflow,\nopenrag-opensearch), disabling/enabling the parent left companions running\nor failed to start them alongside the main container.\n\nChanges:\n- Add dockerCompanions?: string[] field to ServiceDefinitionSeed in @stubrix/shared\n- Add dockerCompanions to openrag service definition (langflow + opensearch)\n- Add getCompanions(serviceId) method to ServiceRegistryService\n- Update enableService to start companions after the main container starts\n- Update disableService to stop companions before stopping the main container\n\nImpact: Disabling OpenRAG from the Settings panel now correctly stops\nall three containers (openrag, openrag-langflow, openrag-opensearch)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptOLXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5WEQABH9bRSdLgqhzOPpCx+kOMel\nVxHnuob5mlBuIaPLKDVptCx8AZwXMYuZJ5VHa72URXMLLllRNMxAirA7TBeF7Ea1\nDn5RRVtc8M6F5EApQzhtBgxGCgfAve3mgNlgoSbKA5l2SSOPvjbokwvAiy95ZA4q\n3kW+ds3Oa8SryMQ+oX54m8JNj1/txuk52isf2oB5qFh4Re9/Z7mXv7CyzaLTL+XC\nBuco+15xFJzozF9FrH+H5k/ryn1jxc1LihOVCUzhTfpnmnv3wDInFa+a1aqkF6+A\npzqEWPZw4puJHzNs95C3Ra2cG6G9dlDp60/vEYNBCDK5/xlCju4Sj2v7/jqRxlW1\nv/hHt+YpHYL65cWh1dZRM2ssCV06BonUcy2R7omQqTbkpeEMKL/KnTfvBm9qZhtS\nAwvkCx/Zw2GIF29OhHbO9W23+JevUMl+CtXjoD/cTgCsDzIURHs/lntSdRWe8zDt\nYER7KA0HFQOkb7yhE3D1Ei2oTfEFS6UleSKMWT4FQ3/pFXgHdZQpOEL9VEXJ0ePZ\n5sdBkk2+uVY/iVm+gVaDP2NTyjM55kB12gYxoez4o1K4kac0Cn6UC3N780iv5Bm0\nOiWyzFxZ+djuzloz0wE/DORJ+kGu6FAEfjASq53eA+QJ+4D2xmWm3eRuMObHDty6\nfo1PnEBZpPPEpRk0NQPX\n=l7WL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-14T04:23:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDg5MzYzMWQ3MzcxMjBhOGJlMWRmODViNGEzZGU0OTYxNGJjMzU2ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8","sha":"318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8"}],"sha":"893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/893631d737120a8be1df85b4a3de49614bc356e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:09:02Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T04:09:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"🐛 fix(intelligence): align service with real OpenRAG API endpoints (#243)\n\nIntelligenceService was calling non-existent endpoints (/query,\n/generate/mock, /generate/data, /index) instead of the actual\nOpenRAG API routes.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace POST /query with POST /chat using { prompt } body\n- Replace POST /generate/mock with POST /chat + WireMock prompt template\n- Replace POST /generate/data with POST /chat + SQL prompt template\n- Replace POST /index with POST /upload_context multipart per file\n- Add OpenRagChatResponse interface for defensive response parsing\n- Add parseMockSuggestion/parseDataSuggestion to extract JSON from LLM text\n- Preserve heuristic fallbacks for offline/no-API-key scenarios\n\nImpact: Intelligence endpoints now call real OpenRAG API correctly;\ngraceful degradation maintained when OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured","tree":{"sha":"1f1c3e1fe57130afd670acedd82a568ede8a88fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/1f1c3e1fe57130afd670acedd82a568ede8a88fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f1c3e1fe57130afd670acedd82a568ede8a88fc\nparent b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773461342 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773461342 -0300\n\n🐛 fix(intelligence): align service with real OpenRAG API endpoints (#243)\n\nIntelligenceService was calling non-existent endpoints (/query,\n/generate/mock, /generate/data, /index) instead of the actual\nOpenRAG API routes.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace POST /query with POST /chat using { prompt } body\n- Replace POST /generate/mock with POST /chat + WireMock prompt template\n- Replace POST /generate/data with POST /chat + SQL prompt template\n- Replace POST /index with POST /upload_context multipart per file\n- Add OpenRagChatResponse interface for defensive response parsing\n- Add parseMockSuggestion/parseDataSuggestion to extract JSON from LLM text\n- Preserve heuristic fallbacks for offline/no-API-key scenarios\n\nImpact: Intelligence endpoints now call real OpenRAG API correctly;\ngraceful degradation maintained when OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptN9eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWPcQACRoxj5TTIcvHavoNapvwsds\nJitU5f1Kabm8rXUa5k6fP7ldK7PlrjtR7Xew31ql/DffpjXpDUWOxrGKCECYW/OB\nz/QxJ7DL7Gv43FzPeAZz55xj/RLyERrY9XgUimNLGOv+ppWMXSKmEZ1FBs/X9WuF\narDeb+kRWBPB5JGUsJVLsImLECrdO/q8jEIPCcuJ6vWO2gzgi46r8xbM3vgMlrMk\nYHf2YwSz/uNNpRM+GfaY+sbf7Y5lRwuFOKGx+G4PYFrOdNQB5ixz/nrBnD8Z1fR3\nZlqKm/+1JmgkTSPiuzXE1yqTpmJy5TAL7kL4fFt/ov9ofVNdJzIiWvO3b3U67Nhz\nUoYd+5ieanJNbtsjHu1a5u+IxF9TL5b/6vzNJMhyxzYGdSpcNK7yOBgRrLmfZRhk\ncWqjneEkgVkuylUsCPal/kZuzK+PKXoh8Z55Ws/OD7o6FHSbGZaRo6Hf0Vvr1O6y\noXNt/c5Pm1OFFi4ufnTjK+NjmDvEl1Q786xhgWRhaoOk8r0pvjKypl+9uUN4N6Jf\nyQ1A665BCEpBbX7Y2Xn9r/9d1BoSWi8qel8eIn50ZOBluVUFfKxcJamFyAMgOjAs\n5O/ZXibYXLkkBVhUWQuebH6Tz4p+o4wSiXSIORnpBNWVyJjNEf3OwzodIFPVQPMK\nfxvhI9IjbyfnK2B2YGy0\n=BJJL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-14T04:09:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDMxOGJiNDVkNTBkMDliYzI2MWQwYTQzZTYzNDY3ODBiOWJiYjc4YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2","sha":"b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2"}],"sha":"318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/318bb45d50d09bc261d0a43e6346780b9bbb78a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T03:56:24Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T03:56:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(openrag): fix OpenRAG stack with companion services and lifecycle improvements (#242)\n\n* 🐛 fix(health): start monitoring on boot and fix Hoppscotch health check\n\nHealth monitoring was never started — startMonitoring() was defined but\nnever called, so health statuses never updated after initial enable.\nHoppscotch HTTP check at localhost:3100/ was failing with non-2xx\nresponses even when the container was running. UI had no polling, so\nstale health statuses persisted until page reload.\n\nChanges:\n- Call health.startMonitoring() in onModuleInit so monitoring begins at startup\n- Run an immediate monitoring cycle on startMonitoring (no delay on first run)\n- Change Hoppscotch health check from HTTP to TCP — port open = healthy\n- Add 15s polling interval in useSettings so UI reflects health updates\n\nImpact: Health status now stays accurate and updates automatically without\nrequiring the user to reload the page\n\n* 🐛 fix(lifecycle): ensure already-enabled services start on API restart\n\nenableService() returns early when row.enabled===1, so containers\nthat were stopped while the API was down were never restarted on boot.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace enableService() call in onModuleInit with ensureServiceRunning()\n- ensureServiceRunning() calls docker.startProfile() directly, bypassing\n  the \"already enabled\" DB guard — safe because startProfile uses --no-recreate\n- Keeps existing health monitoring startup and auto-start logging intact\n\nImpact: Services marked enabled in DB are always restarted when the\nAPI boots, even if their container was stopped\n\n* 🐛 fix(config): correct COMPOSE_FILE_PATH relative to packages/api/ CWD\n\nnest start --watch runs from packages/api/, so resolve(docker-compose.yml)\nexpanded to packages/api/docker-compose.yml instead of the repo root.\n\nChanges:\n- Change COMPOSE_FILE_PATH from docker-compose.yml to ../../docker-compose.yml\n  in .env.example (local .env must be updated manually by each developer)\n\nImpact: DockerComposeService now resolves the correct compose file path\n\n* 🐛 fix(openrag): fix OpenRAG stack with companion services\n\nOpenRAG was unhealthy due to wrong image, missing companion services,\nand an invalid health check URL.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace image with langflowai/openrag-backend, map port 8888→8000\n- Add openrag-langflow companion service (langflowai/openrag-langflow)\n- Add openrag-opensearch companion service (langflowai/openrag-opensearch)\n- Configure discovery.type=single-node, ulimits and heap 512m for OpenSearch\n- Fix OPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD default to meet complexity requirements\n- Add OPENSEARCH_HOST/PORT env vars to backend service\n- Remove incorrect chromadb dependency from openrag service definition\n- Fix health check URL from /health_check to /health\n- Update service schema for correct OpenRAG env vars\n- Document OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD in .env.example with strength warning\n\nImpact: OpenRAG shows healthy and connects to both Langflow and OpenSearch\n\n* ♻️ refactor(lifecycle): isolate container start/stop to single service\n\nstartProfile/stopProfile were starting/stopping all services in a profile,\ncausing unintended side effects when enabling/disabling a single service.\n\nChanges:\n- Add startService(serviceName) method to DockerComposeService\n- Add stopService(serviceName) method to DockerComposeService\n- Replace startProfile with startService in enableService and ensureServiceRunning\n- Replace stopProfile with stopService in disableService\n- Cache getRunningContainers() in getAllStatuses to avoid N parallel docker ps calls\n\nImpact: Enabling/disabling one service no longer affects co-profile services\n\n* 🐛 fix(ui): fix ServiceConfigPage data mapping and navigation guard\n\nConfig page was rendering blank due to three data mapping bugs and a\nuseBlocker incompatibility with BrowserRouter.\n\nChanges:\n- Convert configs array to Record keyed by field key\n- Convert effective configs array to Record keyed by key field\n- Fix history fetch URL (/config/history → /history)\n- Fix history response parsing (API returns { entries, total } not bare array)\n- Remove useBlocker (incompatible with BrowserRouter), replace with manual confirm\n\nImpact: Service config page renders fields and history correctly","tree":{"sha":"a6e50b179dd2b34106bfc87bc526402f84e7929d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/a6e50b179dd2b34106bfc87bc526402f84e7929d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2","verification":{"payload":"tree a6e50b179dd2b34106bfc87bc526402f84e7929d\nparent 09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773460584 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773460584 -0300\n\nfix(openrag): fix OpenRAG stack with companion services and lifecycle improvements (#242)\n\n* 🐛 fix(health): start monitoring on boot and fix Hoppscotch health check\n\nHealth monitoring was never started — startMonitoring() was defined but\nnever called, so health statuses never updated after initial enable.\nHoppscotch HTTP check at localhost:3100/ was failing with non-2xx\nresponses even when the container was running. UI had no polling, so\nstale health statuses persisted until page reload.\n\nChanges:\n- Call health.startMonitoring() in onModuleInit so monitoring begins at startup\n- Run an immediate monitoring cycle on startMonitoring (no delay on first run)\n- Change Hoppscotch health check from HTTP to TCP — port open = healthy\n- Add 15s polling interval in useSettings so UI reflects health updates\n\nImpact: Health status now stays accurate and updates automatically without\nrequiring the user to reload the page\n\n* 🐛 fix(lifecycle): ensure already-enabled services start on API restart\n\nenableService() returns early when row.enabled===1, so containers\nthat were stopped while the API was down were never restarted on boot.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace enableService() call in onModuleInit with ensureServiceRunning()\n- ensureServiceRunning() calls docker.startProfile() directly, bypassing\n  the \"already enabled\" DB guard — safe because startProfile uses --no-recreate\n- Keeps existing health monitoring startup and auto-start logging intact\n\nImpact: Services marked enabled in DB are always restarted when the\nAPI boots, even if their container was stopped\n\n* 🐛 fix(config): correct COMPOSE_FILE_PATH relative to packages/api/ CWD\n\nnest start --watch runs from packages/api/, so resolve(docker-compose.yml)\nexpanded to packages/api/docker-compose.yml instead of the repo root.\n\nChanges:\n- Change COMPOSE_FILE_PATH from docker-compose.yml to ../../docker-compose.yml\n  in .env.example (local .env must be updated manually by each developer)\n\nImpact: DockerComposeService now resolves the correct compose file path\n\n* 🐛 fix(openrag): fix OpenRAG stack with companion services\n\nOpenRAG was unhealthy due to wrong image, missing companion services,\nand an invalid health check URL.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace image with langflowai/openrag-backend, map port 8888→8000\n- Add openrag-langflow companion service (langflowai/openrag-langflow)\n- Add openrag-opensearch companion service (langflowai/openrag-opensearch)\n- Configure discovery.type=single-node, ulimits and heap 512m for OpenSearch\n- Fix OPENSEARCH_INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD default to meet complexity requirements\n- Add OPENSEARCH_HOST/PORT env vars to backend service\n- Remove incorrect chromadb dependency from openrag service definition\n- Fix health check URL from /health_check to /health\n- Update service schema for correct OpenRAG env vars\n- Document OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD in .env.example with strength warning\n\nImpact: OpenRAG shows healthy and connects to both Langflow and OpenSearch\n\n* ♻️ refactor(lifecycle): isolate container start/stop to single service\n\nstartProfile/stopProfile were starting/stopping all services in a profile,\ncausing unintended side effects when enabling/disabling a single service.\n\nChanges:\n- Add startService(serviceName) method to DockerComposeService\n- Add stopService(serviceName) method to DockerComposeService\n- Replace startProfile with startService in enableService and ensureServiceRunning\n- Replace stopProfile with stopService in disableService\n- Cache getRunningContainers() in getAllStatuses to avoid N parallel docker ps calls\n\nImpact: Enabling/disabling one service no longer affects co-profile services\n\n* 🐛 fix(ui): fix ServiceConfigPage data mapping and navigation guard\n\nConfig page was rendering blank due to three data mapping bugs and a\nuseBlocker incompatibility with BrowserRouter.\n\nChanges:\n- Convert configs array to Record keyed by field key\n- Convert effective configs array to Record keyed by key field\n- Fix history fetch URL (/config/history → /history)\n- Fix history response parsing (API returns { entries, total } not bare array)\n- Remove useBlocker (incompatible with BrowserRouter), replace with manual confirm\n\nImpact: Service config page renders fields and history correctly","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptNxoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6wQQAIuq2j/x3WRx8rCLOXn1gxCB\n37Rv/mpRDTptaki0oY2oC1OBCRC6z4qH0mAMN7Vug9OOLT75jyx35I9+JPhWNEI1\nEFg7vN724SiNH1RCp6yEVawApXSxKwijCFRslm9iQ09lzoUS96y2A2vscJAriqRg\nQpTJoAkT+x9VFrJPdVnN4KJvzMhLdIK/Dq/Byb2kp49l80oThmKNhBCp2pEvREpJ\nJeijj4eoKqpUt3N4iYtUdYuV3dzcTKPsgdS+Xrs2LDpf1f5sUf9+mqiX15CWsZlD\nRfMLRoSH/iv7A/x3onw1RTcbq1S4cd6hrNEPy0t4zjlZVi+fmM1zncXdrK4n+q4N\nBVRf19E4HKnGtHLkrMPNPGW7bH7PFRhDR7jPr1e8rX2H1RfqscG9an3K2EWevSIE\n+8tpuLhg/sTouIAgOmniKMAFRR/yIiy9viEdI59jYoIIaxmr5up843UbvCw6ckQZ\nOl+7xYU8BZaAvysI0ONkXjNRhAILm5BK6pC6TUyspuOd5D4jdYEax69TBot5foyp\noMjOkfScH98dN2ElFxsXlXXy29MNSJFd1Y3F1jqDvuE/SfIRWBP9YTs0rycSfMtr\n5xMeSpkg1VREPkSRCxVSzhDV6nKPayC/bjmKPc0U8SKtBtpBrpPHMHoZn4wB1A8U\njI1wBwYq2kPJEAk+fDw4\n=Dvu1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-14T03:56:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKGIwODM3MThhNWFmYWZmNDAxYWM0OTExZDNmZTk1MWM2NjY1YTYwZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf","sha":"09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf"}],"sha":"b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/b083718a5afaff401ac4911d3fe951c6665a60d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T02:03:48Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T02:03:48Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"message":"🐛 fix(ui): prevent duplicate service toggle calls and fix stale pending state\n\nThe void operator on handleToggle discarded the Promise, causing\nServiceToggle pending state to reset immediately instead of awaiting\nthe full API call + refresh cycle. This allowed firing multiple\nenable/disable requests while one was still in flight.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove void from onToggle handler in SettingsPage so Promise propagates\n- Change onToggle types to Promise<void>|void in ServiceGrid, ServiceCard\n- Change onChange type in ServiceToggle to Promise<void>|void\n- await onChange() directly instead of Promise.resolve(onChange())\n- Add res.ok check in toggleService — throw on HTTP error so toggle reverts\n\nImpact: Toggle is disabled for the full duration of the API call;\nduplicate requests are no longer possible","tree":{"sha":"9c53acd6668c9a44e67d82741567b6fc3ce4baaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/9c53acd6668c9a44e67d82741567b6fc3ce4baaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDA5ZjE4NDEzMWUxNjJmZWMyODc3ODZmNDg5OWJlMWE0NGE4NDA3Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b","sha":"37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b"}],"sha":"09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/09f184131e162fec287786f4899be1a44a8407cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T02:03:36Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T02:03:36Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"message":"🐛 fix(api): remove false-positive \"already running\" check in startProfile\n\ndocker compose --profile X ps --status running -q returns IDs of all\ndefault-profile containers (Redis, Postgres) regardless of whether the\nprofile-specific container is actually running. This caused startProfile\nto skip up when the target container was stopped.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove the isRunning pre-check from startProfile\n- docker compose up --no-recreate is idempotent and handles already-running\n  containers correctly without needing an extra ps check\n\nImpact: Services now actually start when toggled on in the UI","tree":{"sha":"0911c0240de824bee10e4082b794c52c93200384","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/0911c0240de824bee10e4082b794c52c93200384"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b","node_id":"C_kwDOReiSwNoAKDM3Njk3YjczMTdjYjBlMGFkMDkwZmZjZWQ5MWI3NjhmMDA2NTY3M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commit/015d6ce302d541179a726dd691add87ccb0ba0e0","sha":"015d6ce302d541179a726dd691add87ccb0ba0e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/015d6ce302d541179a726dd691add87ccb0ba0e0"}],"sha":"37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/37697b7317cb0e0ad090ffced91b768f0065673b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-davanco","id":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/015d6ce302d541179a726dd691add87ccb0ba0e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-14T01:22:58Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-14T01:22:58Z","email":"marcelo.davanco@grupoboticario.com.br","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"message":"🐛 fix(infra): set Redis eviction policy to noeviction\n\nBullMQ requires noeviction policy to prevent data loss when memory is\nfull. Changed from allkeys-lru to noeviction.\n\nChanges:\n- Update Redis command in docker-compose.yml\n\nImpact: Eliminates BullMQ eviction policy warnings on startup","tree":{"sha":"7103f1f7c91c2c22db14b156aff50d58d3c53cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/7103f1f7c91c2c22db14b156aff50d58d3c53cc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/015d6ce302d541179a726dd