"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/a31c4583471d0c8f97b488ed246de194ce1eb84e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-13T23:14:19Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-13T23:14:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ Async Job Queue System with BullMQ + Redis (#241)\n\n* 🔧 chore(infra): add Redis service and BullMQ dependencies\n\nAdd Redis 7 to docker-compose with redis/infra profiles and Makefile\ntargets for local dev mode. Install bullmq and ioredis in @stubrix/api.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Redis service to docker-compose.yml with redis and infra profiles\n- Add redis_data volume for persistence\n- Add Makefile targets: dev, infra-up, infra-down, redis-up, redis-down\n- Add REDIS_HOST/PORT/PASSWORD/DB to .env.example\n- Install bullmq and ioredis in @stubrix/api\n\nImpact: Provides queue infrastructure for async job processing\n\n* ✨ feat(shared): add job queue types and exports configuration\n\nDefine shared types for the async job system and fix nodenext module\nresolution with proper exports field.\n\nChanges:\n- Add JobType, JobStatus, JobPriority, StubrixJob, JobAcceptedResponse,\n  JobProgressEvent, JobWebhookPayload, ListJobsQuery, ListJobsResponse\n- Export job types from @stubrix/shared index\n- Add exports field to package.json for nodenext resolution\n\nImpact: Provides type-safe contract for all async job operations\n\n* ✨ feat(api): create JobsModule with BullMQ queue system\n\nImplement core async job infrastructure with BullMQ queues, SSE streaming,\nwebhook callbacks, and processors for snapshots, imports and scenarios.\n\nChanges:\n- Create JobsService with enqueue, status tracking, progress and cancel\n- Create JobsController with GET /jobs, GET /jobs/:id, SSE /jobs/:id/stream\n- Create SnapshotProcessor, ImportProcessor, ScenarioProcessor\n- Register 8 queues (snapshots, imports, scenarios, recording, etc.)\n- Wire JobsModule into AppModule with swagger tag\n- Add @stubrix/shared paths mapping to tsconfig for IDE resolution\n\nImpact: Enables fully async job processing with real-time progress tracking\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert DbSnapshotsService to async with queue support\n\nReplace blocking execFileSync with async execFile and add queue-based\nasync endpoints for snapshot create and restore.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace execFileSync with promisify(execFile) in createPostgresSnapshot\n  and restorePostgresSnapshot\n- Add async endpoints: /db/snapshots/async, /db/snapshots/:name/restore/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n\nImpact: Snapshot operations no longer block the API event loop\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert ImportService to async with queue support\n\nAdd queue-based async endpoints for HAR and Postman import operations.\n\nChanges:\n- Inject JobsService into ImportController\n- Add async endpoints: har-raw/async, postman-raw/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n- Preserve existing synchronous endpoints for backward compatibility\n\nImpact: Large import operations can now run in background without timeout\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert ScenariosService to async with queue support\n\nAdd queue-based async endpoints for scenario capture and restore.\n\nChanges:\n- Inject JobsService into ScenariosController\n- Add async endpoints: capture/async, :id/restore/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n- Fix .gitignore to cover packages/api/data/*.db files\n\nImpact: Scenario operations can now run asynchronously via job queue","tree":{"sha":"f385fe10079879ee5a5a82a41c16f5e16ddff78d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/f385fe10079879ee5a5a82a41c16f5e16ddff78d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/a31c4583471d0c8f97b488ed246de194ce1eb84e","verification":{"payload":"tree f385fe10079879ee5a5a82a41c16f5e16ddff78d\nparent 270dc70739fe0cc8c33408f45cdac79e6a293fd6\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773443659 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773443659 -0300\n\n✨ Async Job Queue System with BullMQ + Redis (#241)\n\n* 🔧 chore(infra): add Redis service and BullMQ dependencies\n\nAdd Redis 7 to docker-compose with redis/infra profiles and Makefile\ntargets for local dev mode. Install bullmq and ioredis in @stubrix/api.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Redis service to docker-compose.yml with redis and infra profiles\n- Add redis_data volume for persistence\n- Add Makefile targets: dev, infra-up, infra-down, redis-up, redis-down\n- Add REDIS_HOST/PORT/PASSWORD/DB to .env.example\n- Install bullmq and ioredis in @stubrix/api\n\nImpact: Provides queue infrastructure for async job processing\n\n* ✨ feat(shared): add job queue types and exports configuration\n\nDefine shared types for the async job system and fix nodenext module\nresolution with proper exports field.\n\nChanges:\n- Add JobType, JobStatus, JobPriority, StubrixJob, JobAcceptedResponse,\n  JobProgressEvent, JobWebhookPayload, ListJobsQuery, ListJobsResponse\n- Export job types from @stubrix/shared index\n- Add exports field to package.json for nodenext resolution\n\nImpact: Provides type-safe contract for all async job operations\n\n* ✨ feat(api): create JobsModule with BullMQ queue system\n\nImplement core async job infrastructure with BullMQ queues, SSE streaming,\nwebhook callbacks, and processors for snapshots, imports and scenarios.\n\nChanges:\n- Create JobsService with enqueue, status tracking, progress and cancel\n- Create JobsController with GET /jobs, GET /jobs/:id, SSE /jobs/:id/stream\n- Create SnapshotProcessor, ImportProcessor, ScenarioProcessor\n- Register 8 queues (snapshots, imports, scenarios, recording, etc.)\n- Wire JobsModule into AppModule with swagger tag\n- Add @stubrix/shared paths mapping to tsconfig for IDE resolution\n\nImpact: Enables fully async job processing with real-time progress tracking\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert DbSnapshotsService to async with queue support\n\nReplace blocking execFileSync with async execFile and add queue-based\nasync endpoints for snapshot create and restore.\n\nChanges:\n- Replace execFileSync with promisify(execFile) in createPostgresSnapshot\n  and restorePostgresSnapshot\n- Add async endpoints: /db/snapshots/async, /db/snapshots/:name/restore/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n\nImpact: Snapshot operations no longer block the API event loop\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert ImportService to async with queue support\n\nAdd queue-based async endpoints for HAR and Postman import operations.\n\nChanges:\n- Inject JobsService into ImportController\n- Add async endpoints: har-raw/async, postman-raw/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n- Preserve existing synchronous endpoints for backward compatibility\n\nImpact: Large import operations can now run in background without timeout\n\n* ♻️ refactor(api): convert ScenariosService to async with queue support\n\nAdd queue-based async endpoints for scenario capture and restore.\n\nChanges:\n- Inject JobsService into ScenariosController\n- Add async endpoints: capture/async, :id/restore/async\n- Async endpoints return HTTP 202 with jobId for progress tracking\n- Fix .gitignore to cover packages/api/data/*.db files\n\nImpact: Scenario operations can now run asynchronously via job queue","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptJpLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASjQQAB7jOkEBPBzODmNa65iwvRYx\nD5FpuxV5dOmZ7jONdPbAZo1wSunUCqnCvXXPd7v/7AerkUQ1/YyBC5kgONqAUDs3\nt+sYF/e2JR9s5+CCL1Fwsbd86E0oUDoGW3wy2LuUTcWxjvMB3HjUQBVbuen7O70+\niMWO+ZGwRnoUE6I9yBTLnv71vkjS8dXoqgr4stxTrD6UI/MHWrD4tMzoFBj9Oltd\nq8LLx6GQo9F1ZvXTx/0nKbqvgO61Ar5oKyZMuvKS5KtGs8raHfTZrP0QHSsBvkrx\neU0IigQU/8zvpVm8fEYbCIjMHaCm9rYwH5oKDNE4sSAfyCMoIVRSVLjw9WpU2HqC\nNSYYivTuobhweiGf15g/aYp7vEw8h4vpeVujyK5gR4OotftJ9p/uwEcM1pL7byV+\naYWAPDRrTpwXTTMoOA0TWuEk5aLlWCzQjiMsYKAjglKOB4pLPdM5FGJJ30qeZcCr\nGeQhnFL1rFY+LQxVeGAOsimcfhwM0xBL7oMcRrKqcGTKfvEZZzvtQaCj75Zmlve8\nE6piHCnlNCW+8qFHSLBILRYxOyH8drbdBCaB66FZs4U6GTSrVfMPupVkZbjNGwcl\nA1mTz+2EZ3Arhqg7ATiivom8wKi98wQvBk9gd6JkUSCjuR+pY9fktcu65QzBG4wh\ntJcmKKo79BMYMctmgseE\n=92Fz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-13T23:14:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/marcelo-dava