ix/commits/3a461c132395b6fcfd9117d1df9916d8eafe97a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-13T17:19:57Z","email":"73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Marcelo Davanço"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-13T17:19:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat(coverage): add Postman collection analysis support (#230)\n\n* 🎨 chore(assets): add favicons, logotipo and vscode-extension resources\n\nAdd all static assets required by the UI and VS Code extension.\n\nChanges:\n- assets/stubrix_base_logotipo.png: Stubrix brand logotipo\n- assets/favicon/: full favicon set (ico, 16x16, 32x32, 192x192, 512x512, apple-touch, webmanifest)\n- packages/api/public/: favicon set served by the NestJS API static files\n- packages/ui/public/: favicon set for Vite dev server\n- packages/vscode-extension/resources/: icon.png + stubrix.svg for the VS Code extension\n- packages/vscode-extension/package-lock.json: lockfile for the extension package\n\nImpact: UI and extension have proper branding assets; favicon shows in browser tabs.\n\n* 🔧 chore(infra): update docker-compose, Makefile, env example and tooling\n\nExpand infrastructure configuration to cover all new platform services.\n\nChanges:\n- docker-compose.yml: add profiles for Kafka/Redpanda, RabbitMQ, GripMock,\n  Pact Broker, Toxiproxy, ChromaDB, OpenRAG, Hoppscotch, Prometheus, Grafana,\n  Jaeger, LocalStack, MinIO, Keycloak, Zitadel\n- Makefile: add make targets for all new service profiles and vscode-extension\n  (vscode-build, vscode-package, vscode-install, windsurf-install)\n- .env.example: add all new env variables (LocalStack, MinIO, Kafka, RabbitMQ,\n  GripMock, Pact, Toxiproxy, AI/RAG, Jaeger, Prometheus, Grafana, Keycloak, Zitadel)\n- .tool-versions: pin nodejs 24.13.0 for asdf/mise version management\n- package.json: bump to v2.5.0, add vscode-extension workspace and build scripts\n- package-lock.json: update lockfile to reflect new workspace member\n\nImpact: All platform services can be started with a single make target;\nfull environment reference available in .env.example.\n\n* 📝 docs(project): update READMEs, UI config and vscode-extension setup\n\nUpdate documentation and UI configuration to reflect v2.3.0+ state.\n\nChanges:\n- README.md: expand with all new features (contracts, chaos, events, protocols,\n  cloud, tracing, metrics, perf, IAM), MCP ecosystem table, IDE extension guide\n  and roadmap from v1.3.1 to v2.3.0\n- packages/api/README.md: add full module structure, API reference tables and\n  environment variables guide\n- packages/shared/README.md: document all exported types including ImportIR\n- packages/ui/index.html: add favicon, apple-touch-icon and webmanifest links\n- packages/ui/vite.config.ts: add @stubrix/db-ui and @stubrix/mock-ui path aliases\n- packages/vscode-extension/package.json: bump to v2.3.0, add sidebar views,\n  6 commands and configuration schema\n- packages/vscode-extension/tsconfig.json: strict TypeScript config for extension\n\nImpact: New contributors have full reference without reading source code;\nVite dev server correctly resolves all monorepo package imports.\n\n* ✨ feat(coverage): add Postman collection analysis support\n\nAdd comprehensive Postman collection coverage analysis to the Stubrix platform.\n\nChanges:\n- coverage.service.ts: add parsePostmanEndpoints() and analyzeFromPostman() methods\n  using existing parsePostman() from import/parsers/postman.parser\n- coverage.controller.ts: add POST /coverage/analyze/postman (file upload) and\n  /analyze/postman-raw (JSON body) endpoints; add Get import to resolve decorator\n- main.ts: increase JSON body parser limit to 10MB for large Postman collections\n- mock-api.ts: add analyzePostman() client method routing to /coverage/analyze/postman-raw\n- CoveragePage.tsx: auto-detect Postman collections via _postman_id or getpostman.com\n  schema; route to correct endpoint; show ''Postman collection detected'' badge\n\nImpact: Users can analyze mock coverage against Postman collections in addition to\nOpenAPI specs, with automatic detection and proper handling of large payloads.","tree":{"sha":"e6c1ddeae88e6b19be4d96f2d7a46f381f308f8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/e6c1ddeae88e6b19be4d96f2d7a46f381f308f8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/3a461c132395b6fcfd9117d1df9916d8eafe97a3","verification":{"payload":"tree e6c1ddeae88e6b19be4d96f2d7a46f381f308f8e\nparent dd7fd40aa005701c27a785fb968f19d7ea1b8c79\nauthor Marcelo Davanço <73924875+marcelo-davanco@users.noreply.github.com> 1773422397 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773422397 -0300\n\n✨ feat(coverage): add Postman collection analysis support (#230)\n\n* 🎨 chore(assets): add favicons, logotipo and vscode-extension resources\n\nAdd all static assets required by the UI and VS Code extension.\n\nChanges:\n- assets/stubrix_base_logotipo.png: Stubrix brand logotipo\n- assets/favicon/: full favicon set (ico, 16x16, 32x32, 192x192, 512x512, apple-touch, webmanifest)\n- packages/api/public/: favicon set served by the NestJS API static files\n- packages/ui/public/: favicon set for Vite dev server\n- packages/vscode-extension/resources/: icon.png + stubrix.svg for the VS Code extension\n- packages/vscode-extension/package-lock.json: lockfile for the extension package\n\nImpact: UI and extension have proper branding assets; favicon shows in browser tabs.\n\n* 🔧 chore(infra): update docker-compose, Makefile, env example and tooling\n\nExpand infrastructure configuration to cover all new platform services.\n\nChanges:\n- docker-compose.yml: add profiles for Kafka/Redpanda, RabbitMQ, GripMock,\n  Pact Broker, Toxiproxy, ChromaDB, OpenRAG, Hoppscotch, Prometheus, Grafana,\n  Jaeger, LocalStack, MinIO, Keycloak, Zitadel\n- Makefile: add make targets for all new service profiles and vscode-extension\n  (vscode-build, vscode-package, vscode-install, windsurf-install)\n- .env.example: add all new env variables (LocalStack, MinIO, Kafka, RabbitMQ,\n  GripMock, Pact, Toxiproxy, AI/RAG, Jaeger, Prometheus, Grafana, Keycloak, Zitadel)\n- .tool-versions: pin nodejs 24.13.0 for asdf/mise version management\n- package.json: bump to v2.5.0, add vscode-extension workspace and build scripts\n- package-lock.json: update lockfile to reflect new workspace member\n\nImpact: All platform services can be started with a single make target;\nfull environment reference available in .env.example.\n\n* 📝 docs(project): update READMEs, UI config and vscode-extension setup\n\nUpdate documentation and UI configuration to reflect v2.3.0+ state.\n\nChanges:\n- README.md: expand with all new features (contracts, chaos, events, protocols,\n  cloud, tracing, metrics, perf, IAM), MCP ecosystem table, IDE extension guide\n  and roadmap from v1.3.1 to v2.3.0\n- packages/api/README.md: add full module structure, API reference tables and\n  environment variables guide\n- packages/shared/README.md: document all exported types including ImportIR\n- packages/ui/index.html: add favicon, apple-touch-icon and webmanifest links\n- packages/ui/vite.config.ts: add @stubrix/db-ui and @stubrix/mock-ui path aliases\n- packages/vscode-extension/package.json: bump to v2.3.0, add sidebar views,\n  6 commands and configuration schema\n- packages/vscode-extension/tsconfig.json: strict TypeScript config for extension\n\nImpact: New contributors have full reference without reading source code;\nVite dev server correctly resolves all monorepo package imports.\n\n* ✨ feat(coverage): add Postman collection analysis support\n\nAdd comprehensive Postman collection coverage analysis to the Stubrix platform.\n\nChanges:\n- coverage.service.ts: add parsePostmanEndpoints() and analyzeFromPostman() methods\n  using existing parsePostman() from import/parsers/postman.parser\n- coverage.controller.ts: add POST /coverage/analyze/postman (file upload) and\n  /analyze/postman-raw (JSON body) endpoints; add Get import to resolve decorator\n- main.ts: increase JSON body parser limit to 10MB for large Postman collections\n- mock-api.ts: add analyzePostman() client method routing to /coverage/analyze/postman-raw\n- CoveragePage.tsx: auto-detect Postman collections via _postman_id or getpostman.com\n  schema; route to correct endpoint; show ''Postman collection detected'' badge\n\nImpact: Users can analyze mock coverage against Postman collections in addition to\nOpenAPI specs, with automatic detection and proper handling of large payloads.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJptEc9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArO0QAID6SBvSpokx+0GtUmnVBjEy\nTf2XHZP2foSEhnCfNOEhfwGpP1g4SjqbaNPvlujFnRxHtUPltvmXGyBJPdntTzVG\ny3nnoP35ouoTN4oh+HtD8V5lW6ve1pFu1dj9GdGinetvcg7ymnY4PTH3cTPA2em3\n+Fq08YHgpbE+mSrz3zqNhT092KV2/dvytS9eIHB7OZn0hM+JcTSjlxsDTDjkWHQN\nOCle8KXFlLsgUulPYOZmJeBmypub9SDgeHFH+aF5bVca+UWp2QxZQWZqBHUCox5n\nRFdDpr7sIOjfLZukMAdxIF7SYc+OGJXWlXDcNPr7g3TbLyfadb6miRTRZPM5r1Nh\nV2Y9GiLG+NxVUlHBlW8UaljUXhybXlArjfuOHY4qkl0PbIRIcGq25nN/KCJfAJpA\nHZW1YAZVXeMYjZdX2463i1LjSDGUVs5rON3o/ZoFbt2dY4SznIPiYo5ZlfEkLdxT\nxPaEZFBezRsJprJYME7Hn+lpaTfwRII7ffBbdNVZeJBofSkkrQyA6Y2qlSXHQzhB\ns7Zgb2zlZ8olXUHMPfbHHVMwDrucAZcd+OK9kp7wsECq+W88wRbiwMM3YAXKaRPJ\nFsJIHmmWdNoTqAwhIOooL+Wvk2VyqqcRYHVAEHSQAThimmoKUyzCHwGlmqodhU0w\n+4Dm9p0fruTpU9Qd3kf+\n=pA89\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-13T17:19:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/we