d":73924875,"login":"marcelo-davanco","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTI0ODc1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/commits/b28a218ebdec41b7f538e86702a6ab6556b136a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-13T01:36:05Z","email":"marcelo.ceribelli@gmail.com","name":"killvorak2"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-13T01:36:05Z","email":"marcelo.ceribelli@gmail.com","name":"killvorak2"},"message":"✨ feat(api): F21 + F22 + F28 — Metrics, Performance Testing, Distributed Tracing (v2.2.0)\n\nImplement Wave 9 milestone covering observability, performance and tracing.\n\nChanges:\n- F21.01: MetricsService — in-memory counters + histograms with Prometheus text format\n- F21.02: GET /api/metrics/health — detailed check of API + Pact + Toxiproxy + RAG\n  with per-service latency measurement\n- F21.03: Prometheus Docker profile ''monitoring'' (:9091) scraping\n  /api/metrics/prometheus at 15s intervals\n  config/prometheus/prometheus.yml pre-configured for stubrix-api\n- F21.04: Grafana Docker profile ''monitoring'' (:3000 admin/admin)\n  with grafana_data volume and dashboards mount\n- F21.05: MetricsController — GET /api/metrics/prometheus, /summary, /health\n  prometheus and grafana_data volumes added to docker-compose.yml\n- F22.01: PerformanceService + k6 Docker profile (reuses Redpanda profile)\n- F22.02: 3 built-in k6 scripts: smoke (1 VU/30s), load (20 VU ramp),\n  stress (100 VU ramp to break point)\n- F22.03: saveBaseline() + compareBaseline() with 20% p95/p99 regression\n  threshold and 1% absolute error rate gate\n- F22.04: PerformanceController — GET/POST /api/performance/scripts,\n  GET :id/export (JS download), GET/POST /api/performance/baselines,\n  POST :id/compare\n- F22.05: 5 MCP tools: perf_list_scripts, perf_create_script,\n  perf_list_baselines, perf_save_baseline, perf_compare_baseline\n- F28.01: Jaeger Docker profile ''jaeger'' (:16686 UI, :4318 OTLP HTTP, :4317 gRPC)\n  with COLLECTOR_OTLP_ENABLED=true\n- F28.02-03: TracingService — startSpan/finishSpan, file-based trace store,\n  OTEL config from env vars (OTEL_ENABLED, OTEL_EXPORTER_ENDPOINT,\n  OTEL_SAMPLING_RATE, OTEL_SERVICE_NAME)\n- F28.04: TracingController — GET /api/tracing/traces, /:traceId,\n  /health, /config\n  4 MCP tools: tracing_list, tracing_get, tracing_health, tracing_config\n- Register MetricsModule + PerformanceModule + TracingModule in AppModule\n- Add metrics/performance/tracing Swagger tags\n- Makefile: monitoring-up/down, jaeger-up/down; all-down + clean updated\n- Add PROMETHEUS_*, GRAFANA_*, JAEGER_*, OTEL_* env vars to .env.example\n\nCloses #146, #147, #148, #149, #150, #151\nCloses #152, #153, #154, #155, #156\nCloses #186, #187, #188, #189\n\nImpact: teams can now monitor Stubrix with Prometheus/Grafana, run k6\nperformance tests with baseline regression detection, and trace distributed\nrequests end-to-end with Jaeger/OpenTelemetry.","tree":{"sha":"0bac5848a5eb37cb544a16cc5c803933a3a188e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/trees/0bac5848a5eb37cb544a16cc5c803933a3a188e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marcelo-davanco/stubrix/git/commits/b28a218ebdec41b7f538e86702a6ab6556b136a6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/73924875?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcelo-davanco/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.gi